WEBVTT


00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
Downloaded @ subs4free.club


00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:37.211
- All personnel,
prepare to disembark.


00:00:37.213 --> 00:00:41.081
Grab what you need and get
to the front of the ship.


00:00:41.083 --> 00:00:42.116
<i>-Attention, vessel!</i>


00:00:42.118 --> 00:00:45.718
<i>You are in violation
of Coalition regulations.</i>


00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.121
What the...?


00:00:47.189 --> 00:00:48.222
<i>Further transgression</i>


00:00:48.224 --> 00:00:52.325
<i>will be considered
a declaration of war!</i>


00:00:52.662 --> 00:00:55.061
<i>Deactivate your
light-speed engines</i>


00:00:55.063 --> 00:00:57.731
<i>and prepare to be boarded!</i>


00:00:57.733 --> 00:00:59.967
- Ajax, tell me
you're in position.


00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:01.401
We're coming in hot!


00:01:01.403 --> 00:01:04.137
And we got company.


00:01:13.915 --> 00:01:19.352
Look, buddy. I need you to hear
me out. I'm not your enemy.


00:01:19.354 --> 00:01:21.755
-Yield.


00:01:21.757 --> 00:01:23.790
-Screw it.


00:01:31.933 --> 00:01:34.434
Ajax, where are you?
We're ready for pickup!


00:01:34.436 --> 00:01:37.470
<i>- You didn't tell me there
was gonna be a Paladin.</i>


00:01:37.472 --> 00:01:38.705
<i>Too much risk!</i>


00:01:38.707 --> 00:01:41.007
- Ajax, you leave us
out here, we're dead!


00:01:41.009 --> 00:01:41.974
We need your ship!


00:01:41.976 --> 00:01:44.009
<i>- You've got a ship, use it!</i>


00:01:44.011 --> 00:01:47.245
- That wasn't part of
the plan, Ajax!


00:01:47.247 --> 00:01:49.348
Ajax!


00:01:52.487 --> 00:01:55.388
- Disengage the engines
and step away from the console.


00:01:55.390 --> 00:02:01.027
- I can't, or everyone
on this ship will die!


00:02:01.029 --> 00:02:04.030
-Commander Corbryn...


00:02:04.032 --> 00:02:05.864
I don't understand.


00:02:05.866 --> 00:02:07.967
The Coalition reported
this ship stolen.


00:02:07.969 --> 00:02:09.401
Why are you so far off course?


00:02:09.403 --> 00:02:12.337
Commander Corbryn,
by Order of the Coalition,


00:02:12.339 --> 00:02:13.840
stop this ship now!


00:02:13.842 --> 00:02:16.341
- We no longer answer to
the Coalition of Planets.


00:02:16.343 --> 00:02:18.744
- Treason, Commander!


00:02:18.746 --> 00:02:20.012
This is an act of war!


00:02:20.014 --> 00:02:22.447
- The Coalition aren't
the good guys anymore.


00:02:22.449 --> 00:02:24.883
You're a Paladin!
Can't you see that?


00:02:24.885 --> 00:02:28.120
- War against the Coalition
is a fight you cannot win.


00:02:28.122 --> 00:02:30.355
- Well, we don't want a fight.
We want out!


00:02:30.357 --> 00:02:33.225
We want a planet of our own
and we're not turning back,


00:02:33.227 --> 00:02:34.359
not when we're this close.


00:02:34.361 --> 00:02:38.230
- This close to what?
There's nothing...


00:02:39.466 --> 00:02:41.900
Nothing out there.


00:02:43.537 --> 00:02:45.937
- I'm trusting you to
do the right thing.


00:02:45.939 --> 00:02:49.407
Coalition doesn't know it's here
and they don't have to.


00:02:50.444 --> 00:02:51.408
-It's impossible.


00:02:51.410 --> 00:02:55.981
The Coalition has no records
of a planet in this sector.


00:02:55.983 --> 00:02:58.483
- The planet's naturally
undetectable by sensors,


00:02:58.485 --> 00:02:59.818
completely cloaked.


00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.252
I'm the only one
that knows how to find it.


00:03:01.254 --> 00:03:04.421
But this ship will lead them
right to us if you don't help!


00:03:04.423 --> 00:03:06.458
In a moment, we'll be
in range for the escape pods


00:03:06.460 --> 00:03:07.424
to reach the surface.


00:03:07.426 --> 00:03:09.827
After that, destroy the ship!


00:03:09.829 --> 00:03:11.328
Tell them all
you found was a wreck


00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:13.230
or they'll never
stop looking for us!


00:03:13.232 --> 00:03:16.100
They find us, they'll kill us.


00:03:17.103 --> 00:03:18.036
What are you doing?


00:03:18.038 --> 00:03:21.807
<i>- Long-range connection
established.</i>


00:03:21.809 --> 00:03:22.540
-Oh, shut if off!


00:03:22.542 --> 00:03:25.010
<i>- Paladin, this is
Coalition Command.</i>


00:03:25.012 --> 00:03:27.344
<i>We've got a lock
on this ship's position.</i>


00:03:27.346 --> 00:03:30.247
<i>Go ahead and jump out.
We'll take it from here.</i>


00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:32.983
- Commander, I'm on board
the stolen vessel.


00:03:32.985 --> 00:03:35.219
Permission to negotiate
terms for surrender.


00:03:35.221 --> 00:03:38.455
<i>-Negative.
Command advises
immediate evacuation.</i>


00:03:38.457 --> 00:03:40.124
<i>- We will destroy
that ship, Paladin.</i>


00:03:40.126 --> 00:03:42.860
<i>- No!
- Make sure you're not on it.</i>


00:03:42.862 --> 00:03:44.428
- No!


00:03:47.366 --> 00:03:49.033
-Oh! No!


00:03:49.035 --> 00:03:51.135
-What...? What's happening?


00:03:51.137 --> 00:03:52.269
-They're blowing the engines.


00:03:52.271 --> 00:03:54.205
Didn't even
give us time to evacuate.


00:03:54.207 --> 00:03:55.339
I told you!
- No. They won't!


00:03:55.341 --> 00:03:57.608
They wouldn't! It's impossible!
Command, come in!


00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.542
There are innocent people
onboard the vessel!


00:03:59.544 --> 00:04:02.579
- Not even you can get a signal
out this close to the planet.


00:04:02.581 --> 00:04:04.481
There's no time
to get everyone off.


00:04:04.483 --> 00:04:06.015
How many does your ship hold?


00:04:06.017 --> 00:04:06.617
-Not enough.


00:04:06.619 --> 00:04:09.319
Squire, prepare to initiate the
boarding pod's self-destruct...


00:04:09.321 --> 00:04:10.454
-What are you doing?


00:04:10.456 --> 00:04:12.255
- Buying you and your
people time to escape.


00:04:12.257 --> 00:04:14.858
Get them to the front and
I'll separate the engines!


00:04:14.860 --> 00:04:17.927
- Separate...?
- Do it now!


00:04:18.029 --> 00:04:19.563
-All personnel, evacuate now!


00:04:19.565 --> 00:04:22.967
Drop what you're
doing and go... now!


00:04:22.969 --> 00:04:24.167
What about you?


00:04:24.169 --> 00:04:25.168
-Don't worry about me.


00:04:25.170 --> 00:04:30.106
Squire, prepare to initiate
the self-destruct on my command!


00:04:30.108 --> 00:04:31.541
Squire?


00:04:40.352 --> 00:04:42.952
<i>-Security override.</i>


00:06:27.757 --> 00:06:31.192
- Better a few years
late than never.


00:06:46.542 --> 00:06:48.442
Hello?


00:06:54.116 --> 00:06:56.751
-You made it.


00:06:56.753 --> 00:06:58.586
-Ajax...


00:06:58.588 --> 00:07:00.153
No thanks to you.


00:07:00.155 --> 00:07:04.091
- Found that way out
on a frontier planet.


00:07:04.093 --> 00:07:05.226
Word's spreading.


00:07:05.228 --> 00:07:06.459
You're already getting sloppy.


00:07:06.461 --> 00:07:09.229
- What's the point of a haven
if people can't get here?


00:07:09.231 --> 00:07:11.265
-What about the Coalition?


00:07:11.267 --> 00:07:13.666
- Even if they're
smart enough to decode it,


00:07:13.668 --> 00:07:15.435
the coin only gets you here.


00:07:15.437 --> 00:07:17.638
To get to Haven, you need me.


00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:20.140
-What's it made of?


00:07:20.443 --> 00:07:22.108
-That's Haven's little secret.


00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.345
- So what?


00:07:24.347 --> 00:07:25.278
You're their leader.


00:07:25.280 --> 00:07:27.348
- Haven doesn't really
have a leader.


00:07:27.350 --> 00:07:30.351
I'm just the guy that
knows how to get there.


00:07:33.489 --> 00:07:35.655
Hey, buddy.


00:07:35.657 --> 00:07:39.560
-2,756 Novaks


00:07:39.562 --> 00:07:43.063
perished by these hands


00:07:43.065 --> 00:07:48.234
for this Novak to stand
before you today!


00:07:50.639 --> 00:07:53.606
- No need to sic
your Novak on me, Ajax.


00:07:53.608 --> 00:07:58.377
You know, if anything happens
to me, you'll never find Haven.


00:08:00.482 --> 00:08:04.616
You got anything
to drink on this wreck?


00:08:11.826 --> 00:08:15.795
- Don't you want to know how we
survived after you ditched us?


00:08:15.797 --> 00:08:20.199
- Looks like you
survived just fine.


00:08:28.376 --> 00:08:33.745
-Okay. Helper, you're...


00:08:33.747 --> 00:08:36.782
about to be free.


00:08:39.353 --> 00:08:41.221
Feel any different?


00:08:43.390 --> 00:08:45.691
- Excited at the prospect
of leaving the ship


00:08:45.693 --> 00:08:47.359
for the first time.


00:08:47.361 --> 00:08:51.430
Also the looming potential
for imminent death.


00:08:51.432 --> 00:08:52.831
-Yeah.


00:08:53.467 --> 00:08:58.704
Helper, I, uh, have to do this.
You don't.


00:08:58.706 --> 00:09:00.873
I understand if you want
to stay on the ship.


00:09:00.875 --> 00:09:03.709
-Astera, I go wherever you go.


00:09:03.711 --> 00:09:07.546
- Do you mean that or is that
just how you're programmed?


00:09:08.883 --> 00:09:11.383
-Both.


00:09:19.526 --> 00:09:21.692
She would be proud of you now.


00:09:30.670 --> 00:09:32.771
-How do I look?


00:09:32.773 --> 00:09:35.706
-Like your father's daughter.


00:09:35.708 --> 00:09:36.542
- Okay.


00:09:36.544 --> 00:09:40.845
I didn't realize sarcasm was
a part of your programming now.


00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:50.855
-Move!


00:09:52.225 --> 00:09:54.325
- We have searched every
deep space quadrant


00:09:54.327 --> 00:09:57.929
of known Coalition territory
but this one.


00:09:57.931 --> 00:10:00.631
Corbryn is out there somewhere.


00:10:00.633 --> 00:10:01.498
I know it.


00:10:01.500 --> 00:10:03.501
- There's a reason
we haven't searched here.


00:10:03.503 --> 00:10:07.337
The sector is barren.
There's nothing here.


00:10:07.339 --> 00:10:08.773
And we've been led
astray before.


00:10:08.775 --> 00:10:13.543
- I haven't come this far and
this long to merge everything


00:10:13.545 --> 00:10:17.347
on the word of
that rogue criminal!


00:10:18.685 --> 00:10:20.383
We have other assurances.


00:10:20.385 --> 00:10:22.553
We're close.


00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:33.763
-Tryn, privacy.


00:10:36.268 --> 00:10:37.702
-You sure?


00:10:37.704 --> 00:10:39.502
-Yeah, I'm good.


00:10:43.408 --> 00:10:45.609
Ran out of ice
a few systems back.


00:10:45.611 --> 00:10:48.011
- Most come to Haven
with a lot less.


00:10:48.013 --> 00:10:51.781
Sometimes they drift in on
nothing but life support...


00:10:53.685 --> 00:10:55.685
some don't make it at all.


00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.293
Would have been nice


00:11:03.295 --> 00:11:06.463
having an industrial class
freighter all these years.


00:11:06.465 --> 00:11:08.498
-You did all right without it.


00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.735
- There'd be a lot more
haven on Haven by now.


00:11:11.737 --> 00:11:13.803
-I get it.


00:11:13.805 --> 00:11:15.371
-Ajax...


00:11:15.840 --> 00:11:17.307
You left thousands to die.


00:11:17.309 --> 00:11:22.746
- Because you didn't tell me
there was gonna be a Paladin.


00:11:22.748 --> 00:11:24.480
-It was part of the plan.


00:11:24.482 --> 00:11:26.883
-You didn't tell me the plan.


00:11:28.019 --> 00:11:30.386
-Would you have come if I did?


00:11:30.888 --> 00:11:34.456
Look, I just gotta know.


00:11:34.458 --> 00:11:39.662
Why are you here now,
after all these years?


00:11:41.599 --> 00:11:43.799
How can I trust you?


00:11:47.972 --> 00:11:50.472
- You convinced me
to steal this ship.


00:11:50.474 --> 00:11:52.975
You said we'd never get caught!
- We didn't.


00:11:52.977 --> 00:11:55.911
- And ever since then,
I can't even get an icemaker,


00:11:55.913 --> 00:11:58.981
let alone a decent crew
or the much-needed repairs


00:11:58.983 --> 00:12:00.783
for this tub of rust!


00:12:00.785 --> 00:12:02.318
I'm on the run in a ship


00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.054
I can't dock on
a single Coalition planet.


00:12:05.056 --> 00:12:08.891
And nowadays,
that's every planet!


00:12:08.893 --> 00:12:09.692
-Not Haven.


00:12:09.694 --> 00:12:12.328
We welcome everyone,
even pirates.


00:12:12.330 --> 00:12:14.930
- Don't you call me that!
You do not get to call me that!


00:12:14.932 --> 00:12:17.666
You know I started out legit!


00:12:17.668 --> 00:12:21.837
And you know
Paladins kill pirates!


00:12:23.440 --> 00:12:25.873
How was I supposed
to know he was on our side


00:12:25.875 --> 00:12:28.609
if you didn't tell me?


00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:38.453
You ask me how can you trust me.


00:12:40.391 --> 00:12:42.657
How can I trust you?


00:12:45.395 --> 00:12:47.028
-Because...


00:12:48.431 --> 00:12:50.898
sounds like we need each other.


00:12:54.738 --> 00:12:57.739
We call this Mana.


00:12:57.741 --> 00:13:00.041
There's a lot more
where that came from.


00:13:00.043 --> 00:13:03.411
We convert it to everything
from food to star fuel.


00:13:03.413 --> 00:13:06.147
But we're limited in
the ways of transporting it,


00:13:06.149 --> 00:13:10.585
being as we only have what came
down with us in the escape pods.


00:13:10.587 --> 00:13:14.821
But with you here,
with this ship,


00:13:14.823 --> 00:13:16.457
we can start expanding.


00:13:16.459 --> 00:13:18.993
We set up a supply run,
we get what we need


00:13:18.995 --> 00:13:20.094
to finish what we started,


00:13:20.096 --> 00:13:22.830
bring more people
to Haven, everything!


00:13:22.832 --> 00:13:24.030
We can get back on track!


00:13:24.032 --> 00:13:28.068
We can make this planet
what it was supposed to be!


00:13:29.439 --> 00:13:31.671
What do you say?


00:13:32.876 --> 00:13:34.574
To pirates?


00:13:41.083 --> 00:13:42.949
-To pirates.


00:13:45.988 --> 00:13:46.787
-All right.


00:13:46.789 --> 00:13:49.756
Lucky for us,
Mana in its natural form


00:13:49.758 --> 00:13:50.957
emits a sort of radiation.


00:13:50.959 --> 00:13:53.527
It's harmless to us, but
it's hell on ship sensors.


00:13:53.529 --> 00:13:55.862
One of the first things
we did was to figure out a way


00:13:55.864 --> 00:13:59.699
to counteract the disruption
with a frequency code


00:13:59.701 --> 00:14:03.803
that only a few of us knows...


00:14:08.977 --> 00:14:10.811
Welcome to Haven.


00:14:28.529 --> 00:14:31.964
I'll show you around when
my guys fix up your ship.


00:14:31.966 --> 00:14:33.065
Don't worry about the Coalition.


00:14:33.067 --> 00:14:34.934
The only way they'd find you
now is with some sort


00:14:34.936 --> 00:14:36.937
of two-way signal beacon
strong enough


00:14:36.939 --> 00:14:38.237
to get through
the radiation field.


00:14:38.239 --> 00:14:41.006
Even then, you know, you come
outta light-speed wrong,


00:14:41.008 --> 00:14:43.809
liable to blow us all to hell.


00:14:49.183 --> 00:14:50.649
-Did you catch all that?


00:14:50.651 --> 00:14:53.586
- Is he Haven's leader?
- No.


00:14:53.588 --> 00:14:56.555
Just the guy that knows
how to get there.


00:14:56.557 --> 00:14:57.223
-We copy.


00:14:57.225 --> 00:14:59.892
The Coalition thanks
you, Captain.


00:15:00.127 --> 00:15:04.597
- Do you realize
what you've just done?


00:15:04.599 --> 00:15:06.599
-Pirate.


00:15:10.905 --> 00:15:15.039
- There. Sir, we've
located the pirate.


00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:15.741
Shall I...


00:15:15.743 --> 00:15:17.942
- I think battle stations,
please.


00:15:17.944 --> 00:15:20.279
And see if you can find Astera.


00:15:20.281 --> 00:15:23.781
I would like her
to be here for this.


00:15:38.132 --> 00:15:40.265
- Your father wants to see
you on the Control Deck.


00:15:40.267 --> 00:15:43.701
- I'll be right there.
- No. I'll take you there now.


00:15:43.703 --> 00:15:45.803
-Lead the way.


00:15:48.608 --> 00:15:51.576
- How far can you
project that thing?


00:15:51.578 --> 00:15:52.310
-We'll find out.


00:15:52.312 --> 00:15:55.079
- You know, it's an important
day for my father.


00:15:55.081 --> 00:15:58.249
-Mm-hmm, and for you, I'm sure.


00:15:58.251 --> 00:16:01.286
After all, your entire life


00:16:01.288 --> 00:16:03.855
has been a journey
leading to this place.


00:16:03.857 --> 00:16:08.860
I imagine this planet holds
some significance for you...


00:16:10.597 --> 00:16:12.796
as it did your mother.


00:16:14.868 --> 00:16:15.966
What?


00:16:15.968 --> 00:16:17.168
No juvenile pranks this time?


00:16:17.170 --> 00:16:21.872
No petty, ineffectual
protest in her honor?


00:16:21.874 --> 00:16:25.275
I half expected you'd reroute
the food synthesizers again


00:16:25.277 --> 00:16:28.145
or increase
the artificial gravity.


00:16:28.147 --> 00:16:32.149
I have to say, I'm disappointed.


00:16:32.618 --> 00:16:36.254
- Then you're gon...
really... love th...


00:16:38.123 --> 00:16:40.258
-Where's Astera?


00:16:51.904 --> 00:16:54.237
- Sir, I've located
your daughter.


00:16:54.239 --> 00:16:58.008
She's onboard an escape pod
headed towards the planet.


00:16:58.010 --> 00:17:00.110
-Get up here!


00:17:09.722 --> 00:17:11.220
-He knows.


00:17:11.222 --> 00:17:12.222
-That's good.


00:17:12.224 --> 00:17:15.759
He won't attack if
I'm down there, right?


00:17:15.761 --> 00:17:18.295
-I'm ready to address them.


00:17:18.297 --> 00:17:19.930
Make sure they can hear me.


00:17:19.932 --> 00:17:22.399
Attention, enemies
of the Coalition.


00:17:22.401 --> 00:17:28.338
<i>This is Lord Malastor.
You have been lied to.</i>


00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:30.339
This planet is no haven.


00:17:30.341 --> 00:17:33.376
It's land and resources
are property


00:17:33.378 --> 00:17:34.878
of the Coalition of Planets.


00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:38.948
<i>There is no corner of the
galaxy that the arms of the
Coalition</i>


00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:43.352
<i>cannot reach, and today
I am its hand.</i>


00:17:44.089 --> 00:17:46.789
It'll be up to the leaders
among you


00:17:46.791 --> 00:17:49.392
to determine whether
this hand remains


00:17:49.394 --> 00:17:51.227
open in friendship


00:17:51.229 --> 00:17:54.030
or crushes you in its grasp!


00:17:54.032 --> 00:17:57.199
You have 24 hours
to surrender the planet


00:17:57.201 --> 00:18:00.770
or suffer the consequences.


00:18:00.772 --> 00:18:03.372
Choose wisely.


00:18:07.345 --> 00:18:08.944
Establish a blockade.


00:18:08.946 --> 00:18:11.313
Not a single ship gets out!


00:18:11.315 --> 00:18:13.349
And, Zelus...


00:18:14.819 --> 00:18:16.919
Find my daughter.


00:18:23.394 --> 00:18:24.427
-What's taking so long?


00:18:24.429 --> 00:18:25.861
You get that Mana
cleaned out yet?


00:18:25.863 --> 00:18:31.433
- The reward is mighty,
but this Novak is mightier.


00:18:31.435 --> 00:18:34.302
There's one crate left.


00:18:34.304 --> 00:18:36.938
-Then get it and let's go!


00:18:44.314 --> 00:18:47.716
- System log shows Commander
Corbryn should still be onboard.


00:18:47.718 --> 00:18:49.317
-Lead the way, and hurry.


00:18:49.319 --> 00:18:51.219
-This way!


00:18:51.221 --> 00:18:54.422
- Ah, you're turning me in
and you're robbing me?


00:18:54.926 --> 00:18:56.391
- You let a pirate
onto your spaceport.


00:18:56.393 --> 00:18:58.394
What did you think
was gonna happen?


00:18:58.396 --> 00:19:01.464
- I didn't think you'd
clean out my entire supply!


00:19:01.466 --> 00:19:06.401
Haven needs that Mana!
The galaxy needs it!


00:19:06.403 --> 00:19:08.236
-I didn't want this contract.


00:19:08.238 --> 00:19:10.972
I got caught!


00:19:11.074 --> 00:19:15.844
It was me or you, and
I'm always gonna pick me.


00:19:15.846 --> 00:19:18.079
And I'm always gonna profit.


00:19:18.081 --> 00:19:21.382
- Is that what you
tell yourself, Captain?


00:19:21.384 --> 00:19:24.853
You think they're gonna
honor some pirate's contract,


00:19:24.855 --> 00:19:27.489
you got a nasty surprising
coming to you.


00:19:27.491 --> 00:19:28.389
-Captain Ajax!


00:19:28.391 --> 00:19:29.490
My father sends his regards,


00:19:29.492 --> 00:19:30.992
but he's preoccupied
with the assault.


00:19:30.994 --> 00:19:32.359
It's his wish that
you release the prisoner


00:19:32.361 --> 00:19:35.130
into my custody for the
completion of your contract.


00:19:35.132 --> 00:19:37.232
-And who's your father?


00:19:37.234 --> 00:19:38.465
-Lord Malastor, of course.


00:19:38.467 --> 00:19:40.101
And on behalf of
the Coalition of Planets,


00:19:40.103 --> 00:19:42.803
he'd like to thank you
for a job well done.


00:19:42.805 --> 00:19:43.338
-Uh-huh.


00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:47.975
- He'd also like to pardon you
for any past transgressions.


00:19:48.911 --> 00:19:53.148
- So, Malastor sent
his only daughter


00:19:53.150 --> 00:19:57.050
into enemy territory for him.


00:19:57.052 --> 00:19:58.886
-You be glad he did.


00:19:58.888 --> 00:20:00.420
He might not be so understanding


00:20:00.422 --> 00:20:03.023
over your plundering
Coalition property.


00:20:03.025 --> 00:20:06.860
I'm willing to forgive it
for a job well done.


00:20:06.862 --> 00:20:08.295
- I'll just call and confirm.


00:20:08.297 --> 00:20:09.863
- I wouldn't.
- I'm gonna.


00:20:09.865 --> 00:20:11.331
-Allow me.


00:20:12.067 --> 00:20:13.367
Father, forgive me
for interrupting...


00:20:13.369 --> 00:20:15.401
<i>I thought I sent
you to retrieve the prisoner.</i>


00:20:15.403 --> 00:20:18.038
<i>Was I not clear enough
or can you not handle it?</i>


00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:20.541
- I'm aboard the Bounty
with Captain Ajax.


00:20:20.543 --> 00:20:22.242
She wishes to confirm
your orders.


00:20:22.244 --> 00:20:25.111
<i>I will not be
questioned by a lawless pirate!</i>


00:20:25.113 --> 00:20:28.214
<i>Tell this self-serving captain
that she can turn over</i>


00:20:28.216 --> 00:20:30.117
<i>Commander Corbryn or she can die</i>


00:20:30.119 --> 00:20:32.920
<i>with the rest of the criminals.</i>


00:20:32.922 --> 00:20:35.222
-Fine.


00:20:37.225 --> 00:20:39.459
Get him off my ship then.


00:20:39.461 --> 00:20:42.162
He's not worth the trouble.


00:20:45.534 --> 00:20:47.300
- Wait!
- Hey!


00:20:47.302 --> 00:20:49.402
It's for your own good.


00:20:50.605 --> 00:20:53.105
Come on.


00:20:53.842 --> 00:20:56.275
- Uh, hi.
I'm Corbryn.


00:20:56.277 --> 00:20:57.109
-Astera Malastor.


00:20:57.111 --> 00:20:59.045
- Yeah. I know who you are.
Where we going?


00:20:59.047 --> 00:21:00.379
-We have to get off this ship.


00:21:00.381 --> 00:21:02.548
Launch your fleet!
Activate your defenses!


00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:03.349
Fight back?


00:21:03.351 --> 00:21:04.884
- Haven doesn't really
have a fleet.


00:21:04.886 --> 00:21:06.986
I mean, the people who
come here are refugees,


00:21:06.988 --> 00:21:08.087
you know, farmers, smugglers.


00:21:08.089 --> 00:21:10.156
Some are ex-Coalition,
but not enough.


00:21:10.158 --> 00:21:11.224
Even if we got 'em all to fight,


00:21:11.226 --> 00:21:12.859
we'd just be sending
them to their deaths.


00:21:12.861 --> 00:21:14.493
-Then what do you have?


00:21:14.495 --> 00:21:15.428
-We have a Paladin.


00:21:15.430 --> 00:21:17.029
- All the Paladins are dead.


00:21:17.031 --> 00:21:19.098
- He's not.
At least, I don't think he is.


00:21:19.100 --> 00:21:20.433
He helped save us
when the Coalition tried


00:21:20.435 --> 00:21:22.101
to blow up the ship
that brought us here.


00:21:22.103 --> 00:21:23.970
He's been in hyper-sleep
ever since.


00:21:23.972 --> 00:21:26.571
- Then why didn't you
wake him up before now?


00:21:26.573 --> 00:21:27.440
-We never had to.


00:21:27.442 --> 00:21:29.507
And historically, the Order
of the Paladins


00:21:29.509 --> 00:21:30.643
are loyal to the Coalition.


00:21:30.645 --> 00:21:32.577
- Or you could be handing
my father the planet


00:21:32.579 --> 00:21:34.413
if this guy decides
to turn you in!


00:21:34.415 --> 00:21:35.447
-He won't. Trust me.


00:21:35.449 --> 00:21:37.984
There wouldn't be a Haven
if it wasn't for this guy.


00:21:37.986 --> 00:21:39.417
Only reason we didn't wake
him up before now


00:21:39.419 --> 00:21:41.286
is because I thought it
would somehow


00:21:41.288 --> 00:21:42.254
bring the Coalition here,


00:21:42.256 --> 00:21:44.156
which obviously isn't
an issue anymore.


00:21:44.158 --> 00:21:46.893
He's our last hope,
you know, sort of a


00:21:46.895 --> 00:21:48.493
"break glass in case of"
scenario.


00:21:48.495 --> 00:21:50.462
- Okay.
So what's the next step?


00:21:50.464 --> 00:21:51.897
-Well, we got to get up to him.


00:21:51.899 --> 00:21:54.065
Where's your ship?
- Where's your ship?


00:21:54.067 --> 00:21:55.433
- My ship?
It's on this ship.


00:21:55.435 --> 00:21:56.402
The pirates have it.


00:21:56.404 --> 00:21:57.969
- The pirates
I just saved you from?


00:21:57.971 --> 00:22:02.308
- Yeah. Don't worry.
I got a plan.


00:22:02.610 --> 00:22:03.909
-We're not leaving?


00:22:03.911 --> 00:22:05.076
- Your father will
have established


00:22:05.078 --> 00:22:06.144
an orbital blockade by now.


00:22:06.146 --> 00:22:09.247
- I got a plan that works
for that too, Pixels.


00:22:09.583 --> 00:22:14.085
- Blockade doesn't apply to me,
my ship, or my crew.


00:22:14.087 --> 00:22:15.186
My contract's complete.


00:22:15.188 --> 00:22:16.621
Let us through and
we'll be on our way.


00:22:16.623 --> 00:22:17.689
<i>Can't do that, Captain.</i>


00:22:17.691 --> 00:22:21.158
<i>Lord Malastor
has issued strict orders.</i>


00:22:21.160 --> 00:22:22.193
<i>No ships in or out.</i>


00:22:22.195 --> 00:22:26.031
- Like hell, I'm getting
stuck on this rock!


00:22:26.033 --> 00:22:28.433
Put him on!


00:22:31.638 --> 00:22:34.038
<i>You're trying
my patience, pirate!</i>


00:22:34.040 --> 00:22:35.507
<i>You're surrounded.
You can't escape.</i>


00:22:35.509 --> 00:22:38.476
- Then tell these idiots to
open up and let me through,


00:22:38.478 --> 00:22:39.576
and I'll be out of your hair.


00:22:39.578 --> 00:22:41.479
<i>- You'll be allowed
through the blockade</i>


00:22:41.481 --> 00:22:44.649
<i>once you deliver the rebel
leader per our contract.</i>


00:22:44.651 --> 00:22:48.219
- I just turned him over.
Check with your daughter.


00:22:48.221 --> 00:22:49.553
<i>-With my... what did you say?</i>


00:22:49.555 --> 00:22:52.022
<i>When was this? Where?</i>


00:23:00.534 --> 00:23:01.665
-Whoa! What are you doing?


00:23:01.667 --> 00:23:03.568
-Gonna blast the doors open.


00:23:03.570 --> 00:23:05.336
-No, you're not.


00:23:05.338 --> 00:23:07.671
I've got it. Helper?


00:23:10.576 --> 00:23:11.642
-Hello.


00:23:18.985 --> 00:23:21.485
- What are you doing?
- Well, there's no way


00:23:21.487 --> 00:23:23.754
we'll make it past that blockade
with normal thrusters.


00:23:24.056 --> 00:23:26.290
Gonna have to jump us
into light-speed.


00:23:26.292 --> 00:23:27.424
-Have you done that before?


00:23:27.426 --> 00:23:29.760
- Never from inside
a cargo freighter.


00:23:29.762 --> 00:23:32.495
Strap in.
- To what?


00:23:37.737 --> 00:23:40.671
<i>Answer me, Ajax!
What's going on?</i>


00:23:40.673 --> 00:23:43.407
<i>What happened? Come in!</i>


00:23:52.551 --> 00:23:55.084
-The cowards fled!


00:23:55.086 --> 00:23:57.520
- Take some ships and find them!


00:23:57.522 --> 00:23:59.156
And send some to Haven.


00:23:59.158 --> 00:24:00.723
-What happened?


00:24:00.725 --> 00:24:02.692
- We've lost contact
with the blockade.


00:24:02.694 --> 00:24:05.195
And we're no longer receiving
signal from the Bounty.


00:24:05.197 --> 00:24:08.664
- Delay the assault until
my daughter's been found!


00:24:09.467 --> 00:24:11.435
-Hey, Helper.


00:24:12.604 --> 00:24:13.669
-You okay?


00:24:13.671 --> 00:24:15.671
-You need more seatbelts.


00:24:17.442 --> 00:24:19.042
Where are we?


00:24:19.044 --> 00:24:21.110
-The Past.


00:24:23.615 --> 00:24:26.582
-Think you can get over there?


00:24:34.692 --> 00:24:37.627
Helper?
Did you get there?


00:24:37.629 --> 00:24:38.628
<i>I'm inside.</i>


00:24:38.630 --> 00:24:42.731
- Okay, great.
I'll dock us.


00:24:53.678 --> 00:24:54.544
-Is that him?


00:24:54.545 --> 00:24:57.380
Yeah, that's him.


00:25:08.492 --> 00:25:10.192
-Have you been here before?


00:25:10.194 --> 00:25:12.795
- Only once to make
sure he wasn't dead.


00:25:13.664 --> 00:25:16.631
Planet's distortion field
must have scrambled his ship.


00:25:16.633 --> 00:25:20.202
If I use a certain frequency...


00:25:27.478 --> 00:25:30.645
- It seems we're receiving
a new code,


00:25:30.647 --> 00:25:33.181
an old Coalition code.


00:25:33.183 --> 00:25:35.650
Someone's talking to us.


00:25:35.652 --> 00:25:37.585
-Who?


00:25:37.587 --> 00:25:39.488
<i>What's it say?</i>


00:25:39.490 --> 00:25:41.722
-Peace before order.


00:26:00.476 --> 00:26:02.209
What's wrong with him?


00:26:09.585 --> 00:26:10.885
-Don't touch anything.


00:26:10.887 --> 00:26:12.586
<i>We found him.</i>


00:26:12.588 --> 00:26:15.589
<i>Take him out.</i>


00:26:19.629 --> 00:26:20.861
-This could actually work.


00:26:20.863 --> 00:26:23.497
- Yeah. Let's just hope
he's on our side.


00:26:23.499 --> 00:26:26.300
Go see what you can find out.


00:26:41.217 --> 00:26:42.182
Hi. I'm Astera Mala...


00:26:42.184 --> 00:26:46.587
- Astera Malastor,
daughter of Lord Malastor.


00:26:46.589 --> 00:26:47.388
Greetings.


00:26:47.390 --> 00:26:51.591
I am Denz Atreus, Paladin
of star-sector Epsilon 27.


00:26:51.593 --> 00:26:56.664
And you are Commander...
Commander Corbryn.


00:26:57.632 --> 00:26:58.565
You made it.


00:26:58.567 --> 00:27:01.734
- Yeah.
- Step back.


00:27:03.339 --> 00:27:06.839
The Commander is a good man,
if a little misguided.


00:27:06.841 --> 00:27:10.376
Although admittedly,
I've only known him briefly.


00:27:10.378 --> 00:27:12.680
I will ensure that
he is treated fairly.


00:27:12.682 --> 00:27:14.681
I've synced
with Coalition Command.


00:27:14.683 --> 00:27:17.784
Rest assured, you will be
with your father in a moment


00:27:17.786 --> 00:27:21.421
and we can finally settle
this matter once and for all.


00:27:21.423 --> 00:27:23.423
-No. You don't understand.


00:27:23.425 --> 00:27:25.625
There's gonna be a war.


00:27:26.695 --> 00:27:27.994
Whoa!
- Hey!


00:27:27.996 --> 00:27:29.462
- Hey, stop!
What are you doing?


00:27:29.464 --> 00:27:32.932
- The path to order lies
only through peace.


00:27:32.934 --> 00:27:34.466
Once I've delivered Corbryn,


00:27:34.468 --> 00:27:36.269
negotiations for
surrender may begin.


00:27:36.271 --> 00:27:39.806
- There's not gonna be peace.
My father doesn't negotiate.


00:27:39.808 --> 00:27:41.574
- Denz, if you turn me in,
I'm dead.


00:27:41.576 --> 00:27:43.875
- If you don't get us
to the surface right now,


00:27:43.877 --> 00:27:44.811
people are going to die.


00:27:44.813 --> 00:27:47.312
- No harm will befall
either of you


00:27:47.314 --> 00:27:48.748
while you're
under my protection!


00:27:48.750 --> 00:27:51.284
The same goes for the planet!


00:27:51.286 --> 00:27:52.818
I give you my word.


00:27:52.820 --> 00:27:57.957
You have nothing to fear from
the Coalition of the Planets.


00:27:58.792 --> 00:28:00.893
-Helper! Now!


00:28:01.396 --> 00:28:04.430
-Helper! Ready an escape pod.


00:28:04.833 --> 00:28:07.533
-That was ill-advised.


00:28:13.307 --> 00:28:17.476
- Sir, we're being hailed
in an old Coalition frequency,


00:28:17.478 --> 00:28:20.379
vessel designation "Honor".


00:28:20.381 --> 00:28:22.714
It's a Paladin.


00:28:24.818 --> 00:28:26.517
-So it's true.


00:28:26.519 --> 00:28:30.389
He's still alive
after all this time.


00:28:30.391 --> 00:28:34.393
I thought you dealt
with the last of them.


00:28:35.329 --> 00:28:36.928
-So did I.


00:28:36.997 --> 00:28:41.433
- Let's hope his
loyalties are in order.


00:28:46.073 --> 00:28:49.641
-See? I told you.


00:28:49.643 --> 00:28:51.575
Peace was never an option.


00:28:51.577 --> 00:28:54.879
What Haven needs
right now is a protector.


00:28:54.881 --> 00:28:55.947
-Haven...


00:28:55.949 --> 00:28:57.615
<i>Paladin,
the Coalition of Planets</i>


00:28:57.617 --> 00:28:59.551
<i>thanks you for your
intervention.</i>


00:28:59.553 --> 00:29:00.918
<i>And I'm personally
in your debt for</i>


00:29:00.920 --> 00:29:02.554
<i>the safe recovery
of my daughter.</i>


00:29:02.556 --> 00:29:04.388
<i>I trust she hasn't given
you too much trouble?</i>


00:29:04.390 --> 00:29:07.725
<i>Where is the rebel leader?
- Somewhere you can't get him!</i>


00:29:07.727 --> 00:29:09.827
<i>Astera,
nothing would please me more</i>


00:29:09.829 --> 00:29:13.698
<i>than to resolve this conflict
without bloodshed,</i>


00:29:13.700 --> 00:29:15.367
Disable their
light-speed engines.


00:29:15.369 --> 00:29:18.470
I don't want them running now
that Astera's this close.


00:29:18.472 --> 00:29:22.406
It seems that surrender
is off the table for now.


00:29:22.408 --> 00:29:25.009
Begin the assault!


00:29:25.411 --> 00:29:26.711
Let's see if they
change their minds.


00:29:26.713 --> 00:29:29.480
- It will be my honor
to lead the attack, sir.


00:29:29.482 --> 00:29:30.348
-No, it won't.


00:29:30.350 --> 00:29:34.417
I need someone that I trust
to retrieve Astera for me.


00:29:34.419 --> 00:29:36.487
-What about the Paladin?


00:29:36.489 --> 00:29:39.023
- Do what you normally
do when you find one.


00:29:39.025 --> 00:29:41.058
Just bring her back!


00:29:42.595 --> 00:29:44.528
Continue the attack!


00:29:45.865 --> 00:29:47.063
-No! Do something!


00:29:47.065 --> 00:29:48.399
-They've disabled the controls!


00:29:48.401 --> 00:29:51.502
- Then go back!
Didn't I just see you fly?


00:29:51.504 --> 00:29:52.103
-In zero-g, yes!


00:29:52.105 --> 00:29:56.072
This is low orbit where
I have gravity to contend with!


00:29:56.541 --> 00:30:00.043
- It's okay, Helper.
You can come out now.


00:30:02.714 --> 00:30:04.948
Think you can get over
to that warship?


00:30:04.950 --> 00:30:06.716
-I can try.


00:30:06.718 --> 00:30:10.054
-That I have not seen yet.


00:30:10.056 --> 00:30:11.488
Is that thing real?


00:30:11.490 --> 00:30:12.522
-She is to me.


00:30:12.524 --> 00:30:17.026
- Attention, Honor.
You are ordered to surrender.


00:30:17.028 --> 00:30:17.894
Lord Malastor...


00:30:17.896 --> 00:30:19.897
I've reached the Paladin ship.


00:30:19.899 --> 00:30:21.431
They're not responding.


00:30:21.433 --> 00:30:22.967
-Then wait.


00:30:25.837 --> 00:30:29.105
-Think out who you help.


00:30:30.041 --> 00:30:31.808
-What?


00:30:31.810 --> 00:30:33.543
-It worked. We have to leave.


00:30:33.545 --> 00:30:35.477
- Wait! Stop!
Where are you going?


00:30:35.479 --> 00:30:36.813
We have to help!
- Look, it's all blown up!


00:30:36.815 --> 00:30:39.949
If we don't retreat now, battle
is over before it even begins!


00:30:39.951 --> 00:30:43.086
Hang on, I'm going to
jump up to lightspeed.


00:30:46.625 --> 00:30:49.025
Zelus,
what was that? What happened?


00:30:49.027 --> 00:30:52.729
<i>Do you have Astera? Zelus?</i>


00:30:56.134 --> 00:30:57.499
-He shot me!


00:30:57.501 --> 00:30:59.536
- Squire, I need a map
of the region


00:30:59.538 --> 00:31:01.771
and a waypoint for
the nearest rebel outpost.


00:31:01.773 --> 00:31:04.139
First imperative is
to secure Corbryn


00:31:04.141 --> 00:31:06.208
and aid in the planet's defense!


00:31:06.210 --> 00:31:07.943
Are you all right?


00:31:07.945 --> 00:31:08.912
-Yes.


00:31:08.914 --> 00:31:13.081
I mean, no, but, yeah.


00:31:13.083 --> 00:31:15.984
I can't believe he just shot me.


00:31:15.986 --> 00:31:17.152
-He shot my ship!


00:31:17.154 --> 00:31:19.621
- Will it be all right?
How bad is it?


00:31:19.623 --> 00:31:22.191
- Oh, she'll fly, but
the repairs will take time,


00:31:22.193 --> 00:31:24.827
time we don't have
if we want to reach Corbryn


00:31:24.829 --> 00:31:26.562
before the Coalition does!


00:31:26.564 --> 00:31:29.665
-Lucky for you, we have help.


00:31:30.935 --> 00:31:32.534
-The ship is sophisticated,


00:31:32.536 --> 00:31:35.871
though the technology
is quite antiquated.


00:31:35.873 --> 00:31:38.073
I'm certain I can
manage the repairs.


00:31:38.075 --> 00:31:40.709
-Can this thing be trusted?


00:31:41.579 --> 00:31:43.211
-This thing's name is Helper.


00:31:43.213 --> 00:31:45.547
- Short for "Hard Light
Projected Retainer",


00:31:45.549 --> 00:31:49.884
though I've come to find
that label somewhat derivative.


00:31:50.086 --> 00:31:52.119
-She's the only person I trust.


00:31:52.121 --> 00:31:56.123
- All right. Then I'll
leave Honor in your hands.


00:31:56.125 --> 00:31:58.793
Excuse my ignorance, Helper.


00:31:58.795 --> 00:32:00.562
-Happy to be of service.


00:32:00.564 --> 00:32:02.864
- Helper, I'm gonna
have to leave you alone


00:32:02.866 --> 00:32:04.999
on the ship for a while.


00:32:05.001 --> 00:32:07.768
-You'll be back.


00:32:19.816 --> 00:32:23.251
<i>Listen up down there:
find him.</i>


00:32:23.253 --> 00:32:27.788
<i>And bring him to me.</i>


00:32:32.295 --> 00:32:34.929
-There's something here.


00:32:34.931 --> 00:32:37.098
-Go check it out.


00:32:46.576 --> 00:32:50.610
- Come on, Ajax.
You can do better than that.


00:32:50.612 --> 00:32:53.014
You won't be needing
this anymore.


00:32:54.049 --> 00:32:56.050
Where is your ship?


00:32:56.752 --> 00:33:00.053
<i>You find him yet?</i>


00:33:00.055 --> 00:33:00.887
-Nice try, Ajax,


00:33:00.889 --> 00:33:04.224
but I think you'll find
you're down a couple pirates.


00:33:09.064 --> 00:33:10.130
-I told you, sir!


00:33:10.132 --> 00:33:11.766
Somehow the Paladin made
the jump to light-speed!


00:33:11.768 --> 00:33:14.635
I tried to disable the engines
before they made the jump.


00:33:14.637 --> 00:33:16.736
- You'd better hope
that's all you did.


00:33:16.738 --> 00:33:19.906
- With all due respect,
Lord Malastor,


00:33:19.908 --> 00:33:22.309
your daughter has clearly
chosen her side.


00:33:22.311 --> 00:33:24.678
-I will not hear another word!


00:33:24.680 --> 00:33:28.582
None of that! Not again.
Not from you.


00:33:28.584 --> 00:33:31.651
Get out of my sight and
don't you dare step foot


00:33:31.653 --> 00:33:35.121
on this deck again
until you've found her.


00:33:48.036 --> 00:33:51.171
- We shouldn't be
too far off now.


00:33:51.173 --> 00:33:52.004
-It's funny.


00:33:52.006 --> 00:33:55.608
Before today, I've only been off
the warship a handful of times.


00:33:55.610 --> 00:33:56.710
We're Haven's only hope,


00:33:56.712 --> 00:34:00.013
and neither of us stepped foot
on the planet until now.


00:34:00.282 --> 00:34:03.083
- That's the very nature
of my order.


00:34:03.085 --> 00:34:05.852
- Then why answer
to the Coalition?


00:34:05.854 --> 00:34:07.987
- My order
predates the Coalition


00:34:07.989 --> 00:34:09.956
by a great many cycles.


00:34:09.958 --> 00:34:11.924
There was a time
when their values


00:34:11.926 --> 00:34:13.826
were in line with our own.


00:34:13.828 --> 00:34:17.763
We helped them grow,
we worked together.


00:34:17.765 --> 00:34:22.335
It pains me now to see them
act with such hostility.


00:34:22.337 --> 00:34:25.070
- My dad thinks
what he's doing is right.


00:34:25.072 --> 00:34:27.006
- There is hope
for your father yet.


00:34:27.008 --> 00:34:30.242
- How?
After what he just did?


00:34:30.244 --> 00:34:32.378
-Well, it's like you said.


00:34:32.380 --> 00:34:34.680
Your father believes
he is right.


00:34:34.682 --> 00:34:36.915
It may be up to
us to provide him


00:34:36.917 --> 00:34:39.084
with the necessary perspective.


00:34:39.086 --> 00:34:42.187
-Denz! It's Zelus!


00:34:42.189 --> 00:34:44.188
He's going for the outpost!


00:34:44.190 --> 00:34:45.190
-We need to find cover.


00:34:45.192 --> 00:34:46.925
- Denz, if he gets to
the outpost and blows it up


00:34:46.927 --> 00:34:47.926
before we find Corbryn,


00:34:47.928 --> 00:34:50.395
we're never gonna make it
before the deadline.


00:34:50.397 --> 00:34:51.964
-He won't.


00:34:51.966 --> 00:34:54.065
Run!


00:34:54.869 --> 00:34:58.971
Astera, get to cover now!
Get to the base!


00:35:03.943 --> 00:35:08.047
Everybody out!
Leave... now!


00:35:08.049 --> 00:35:11.749
I said go!
It's your only chance!


00:35:11.751 --> 00:35:13.819
I'm not...


00:35:13.988 --> 00:35:14.919
This is Astera Malastor.


00:35:14.921 --> 00:35:17.456
Tell my father to lock down
on my position.


00:35:17.458 --> 00:35:20.024
I found the rebels!


00:35:29.369 --> 00:35:33.204
Okay, Corbryn, where am I going?


00:35:33.807 --> 00:35:35.840
Where am I going?


00:35:37.977 --> 00:35:39.877
There!


00:35:44.784 --> 00:35:46.350
-Hey! Hey!


00:35:46.352 --> 00:35:49.854
Hey, wait!
Wait for me!


00:35:49.856 --> 00:35:52.757
Hey! Hey!


00:35:52.759 --> 00:35:55.058
Wait for me!


00:36:01.967 --> 00:36:02.900
You gotta be kidding me.


00:36:02.902 --> 00:36:08.873
<i>Hey, buddy, you think
we'd forget you?</i>


00:36:34.867 --> 00:36:37.501
-That is Paladin technology.


00:36:37.503 --> 00:36:41.404
Tell me, friend,
how did you acquire it?


00:36:41.406 --> 00:36:43.340
-From a Paladin, friend.


00:36:43.342 --> 00:36:46.209
-Paladins serve for life.


00:36:47.913 --> 00:36:49.446
-This one did.


00:36:49.848 --> 00:36:52.215
The order you serve
is no longer.


00:36:52.217 --> 00:36:54.384
I made sure of that myself.


00:36:54.386 --> 00:36:56.986
-My brothers... why?


00:36:56.988 --> 00:37:01.057
- There is only the Coalition
and its enemies.


00:37:01.059 --> 00:37:03.425
Lord Malastor offers
you one last chance


00:37:03.427 --> 00:37:05.162
to prove your loyalty.


00:37:05.164 --> 00:37:07.531
- My order stands
as long as I do.


00:37:07.533 --> 00:37:08.898
I decline!


00:37:08.900 --> 00:37:11.034
-I was hoping you'd say that.


00:37:11.036 --> 00:37:14.404
Hand over the girl
and surrender the outpost!


00:37:14.406 --> 00:37:16.973
- I'm here, Zelus.
I'm right here.


00:37:16.975 --> 00:37:19.976
- Astera?
Good to see you.


00:37:19.978 --> 00:37:21.877
I offer you the same terms.


00:37:21.879 --> 00:37:27.049
Come with me or suffer
the consequences of treason!


00:37:27.051 --> 00:37:29.852
I'm sure you remember
what those are.


00:37:29.854 --> 00:37:30.586
-He's not gonna kill me.


00:37:30.588 --> 00:37:32.856
He does whatever
my father tells him to.


00:37:32.858 --> 00:37:36.091
Isn't that right, Zelus?


00:37:36.093 --> 00:37:37.193
-True.


00:37:37.195 --> 00:37:39.395
I've traveled
to every scum-ridden corner


00:37:39.397 --> 00:37:41.864
of this galaxy with your father.


00:37:41.866 --> 00:37:43.866
He's a good man,


00:37:43.868 --> 00:37:46.268
a true leader...


00:37:46.938 --> 00:37:50.105
but he's grown soft and weak.


00:37:50.875 --> 00:37:52.474
Do you know why?


00:37:52.476 --> 00:37:57.246
It's because of you and
your traitor of a mother!


00:37:58.415 --> 00:38:00.349
-You can't kill me.


00:38:00.351 --> 00:38:03.552
- I'm sure your father
will understand.


00:38:03.554 --> 00:38:06.088
After all, I had no choice,


00:38:06.090 --> 00:38:09.291
overcome with grief
after witnessing


00:38:09.293 --> 00:38:12.228
the murder of his only daughter.


00:38:12.230 --> 00:38:16.564
I had to strike down
the Paladin responsible.


00:38:19.436 --> 00:38:22.270
Say hello to your brothers!


00:38:48.465 --> 00:38:51.566
-Helper! Now!


00:39:07.584 --> 00:39:08.949
-Get us out of here!


00:39:08.951 --> 00:39:09.651
-Where to?


00:39:09.653 --> 00:39:13.554
-I found coordinates
for the rebel base,
inputting now!


00:39:13.556 --> 00:39:14.922
Helper?


00:39:14.924 --> 00:39:15.522
-Setting course.


00:39:15.524 --> 00:39:18.525
<i>Coordinates accepted.</i>


00:39:21.230 --> 00:39:24.564
-Denz, I'm so sorry.


00:39:25.969 --> 00:39:29.070
-All of them... dead.


00:39:29.705 --> 00:39:31.471
-I know.


00:39:31.707 --> 00:39:34.207
I didn't know how to tell you.


00:39:36.645 --> 00:39:40.080
- I will avenge you,
my brothers.


00:39:40.082 --> 00:39:42.516
I swear this.


00:39:50.359 --> 00:39:51.625
-Nice shooting back there.


00:39:51.627 --> 00:39:54.126
- I had ample time
to learn Honor's subsystems.


00:39:54.128 --> 00:39:56.229
She's a wonderful ship.


00:39:57.198 --> 00:39:59.199
-I'm kind of worried about him.


00:40:00.035 --> 00:40:03.536
-Look who we found.


00:40:03.538 --> 00:40:05.272
-Should I shoot them too?


00:40:05.274 --> 00:40:06.572
-I wouldn't, if I were you!


00:40:06.574 --> 00:40:09.242
<i>Ajax!
You let me out of here!</i>


00:40:09.244 --> 00:40:10.109
-Pirates!


00:40:10.111 --> 00:40:14.247
- Come on in.
Let's have a chat.


00:40:15.084 --> 00:40:19.318
- She's not gonna kill him.
My father wants him alive.


00:40:19.320 --> 00:40:22.254
This is must be
one of her tricks.


00:40:22.423 --> 00:40:23.589
She must want something.


00:40:23.591 --> 00:40:27.461
- I would caution you not
to trust these brigands!


00:40:27.463 --> 00:40:29.095
They have no honor.


00:40:29.097 --> 00:40:30.464
-I don't know.


00:40:30.466 --> 00:40:33.332
I mean, you're right,
they're pirates.


00:40:33.334 --> 00:40:36.202
But maybe we can
convince them to help.


00:40:36.204 --> 00:40:37.703
-Unlikely.


00:40:37.705 --> 00:40:40.473
Maintain a safe
following distance.


00:40:40.475 --> 00:40:42.008
I will retrieve Corbryn.


00:40:42.010 --> 00:40:42.608
-Denz, wait!


00:40:42.610 --> 00:40:45.511
You're gonna have to think
outside the box on this one.


00:40:45.513 --> 00:40:47.313
They've got the only thing close


00:40:47.315 --> 00:40:49.614
to a functioning fleet
on this planet.


00:40:49.616 --> 00:40:52.151
Maybe we don't blow it up.


00:40:54.655 --> 00:40:56.389
Maybe we need 'em.


00:40:56.391 --> 00:40:58.690
We have to at least try.


00:40:58.792 --> 00:41:02.160
We have to get to them.


00:41:08.301 --> 00:41:10.503
Where are you taking Corbryn?


00:41:10.772 --> 00:41:15.106
- Oh, he'll stay someplace
near, but far enough.


00:41:16.577 --> 00:41:18.343
In case you try anything,


00:41:18.345 --> 00:41:20.645
he goes boom...


00:41:20.647 --> 00:41:22.448
along with your fancy ship.


00:41:22.450 --> 00:41:25.684
- That man is under
my protection.


00:41:26.219 --> 00:41:31.690
- Well, you've done a fine
job so far, haven't you?


00:41:33.660 --> 00:41:34.659
You gonna call your dad?


00:41:34.661 --> 00:41:37.495
- What's it gonna take
for you to let him go?


00:41:37.497 --> 00:41:38.297
-Let him go?


00:41:38.299 --> 00:41:42.600
He's my ticket out of
this mess just like you are!


00:41:43.637 --> 00:41:45.703
You, I don't really care about.


00:41:45.705 --> 00:41:47.172
-You will!


00:41:47.641 --> 00:41:51.309
- Denz... so we both know you're
not gonna press that then.


00:41:52.079 --> 00:41:53.678
-Oh, I'm plenty tempted,


00:41:53.680 --> 00:41:57.448
but right now he's
my insurance policy for you.


00:41:57.450 --> 00:42:01.386
And you're my insurance
policy for them.


00:42:01.621 --> 00:42:02.854
If it came down to it,


00:42:02.856 --> 00:42:08.226
I'm sure your dad would
appreciate my judgment here.


00:42:09.228 --> 00:42:11.830
- Listen, I know
I lied to you before.


00:42:11.832 --> 00:42:14.599
But you have to believe me now
when I tell you that


00:42:14.601 --> 00:42:16.600
if you give my dad
what he wants,


00:42:16.602 --> 00:42:18.802
your next stop
is Coalition Brig.


00:42:19.472 --> 00:42:22.239
- That's if he lets you
off Haven at all!


00:42:24.478 --> 00:42:26.845
-I have the rebel leader,


00:42:26.847 --> 00:42:31.448
thus fulfilling
my contract twice!


00:42:31.450 --> 00:42:37.654
I have Lord Malastor's daughter
and her gallant protector!


00:42:39.860 --> 00:42:42.827
Hey, you forget already?


00:42:42.829 --> 00:42:43.494
-Denz...


00:42:43.496 --> 00:42:46.630
- I will not be held
hostage by cowards!


00:42:46.632 --> 00:42:53.237
- This Novak does
not fear death!


00:42:54.473 --> 00:42:57.174
- You may hide behind
that button of yours.


00:42:57.176 --> 00:43:01.211
You may even press it,
but if you survive the blast,


00:43:01.213 --> 00:43:05.682
you will have me to contend
with until the end of your days.


00:43:05.684 --> 00:43:08.284
-I'm shaking.


00:43:09.588 --> 00:43:12.789
-Denz, please!


00:43:15.394 --> 00:43:18.562
I know we don't have anything
to negotiate with.


00:43:18.564 --> 00:43:20.897
But I'm telling you,


00:43:20.899 --> 00:43:24.433
my father's not
just gonna let you go free.


00:43:26.905 --> 00:43:30.239
The only way out of
this is to fight.


00:43:42.187 --> 00:43:43.653
-This is ill-advised.


00:43:43.655 --> 00:43:45.221
Why play the pirate's game
and wait


00:43:45.223 --> 00:43:48.391
while our enemies draw near
when I can easily dismantle


00:43:48.393 --> 00:43:49.425
this scrap heap of a ship?


00:43:49.427 --> 00:43:51.794
- Yeah.
Let's call that Plan B, okay?


00:43:51.796 --> 00:43:54.797
Like it or not, she has
the upper hand right now.


00:43:54.799 --> 00:43:57.800
We can't lose Corbryn
and we can't lose Honor.


00:43:57.802 --> 00:44:02.871
So I guess we just have to
wait until she comes around.


00:44:03.975 --> 00:44:05.874
Until then...


00:44:08.546 --> 00:44:12.514
See if you can get to Corbryn
and take care of that bomb.


00:44:12.516 --> 00:44:15.350
Then you can bust us
out of here.


00:44:24.795 --> 00:44:28.663
-Hello? Is someone there?


00:44:28.665 --> 00:44:31.266
Oh, Helper!
Is it just you?


00:44:31.268 --> 00:44:31.766
-Yes.


00:44:31.768 --> 00:44:33.002
Explosion device.
I think I can...


00:44:33.004 --> 00:44:34.903
- Don't touch it!
- But maybe if I just...


00:44:34.905 --> 00:44:35.905
-No, no, no, Helper!


00:44:35.907 --> 00:44:37.539
Let me tell you something
about pirates.


00:44:37.541 --> 00:44:40.842
You can't trust 'em and they're
wiring's slap-dash at best!


00:44:40.844 --> 00:44:43.645
Just don't touch it.


00:44:44.982 --> 00:44:46.514
-Okay, com's open.


00:44:46.516 --> 00:44:49.818
- This is Captain Ajax
of the frigate Bounty


00:44:49.820 --> 00:44:51.519
hailing Lord Malastor.


00:44:51.521 --> 00:44:55.624
- I didn't expect to hear
from you again, Captain.


00:44:55.626 --> 00:44:58.292
You'd better have something
to report to me.


00:44:58.294 --> 00:45:00.662
- I've captured
the rebel leader.


00:45:00.664 --> 00:45:05.867
- Ah, it's about time you
made good on our contract.


00:45:05.869 --> 00:45:08.970
-And I have your daughter.


00:45:09.873 --> 00:45:11.573
-Not bad for a pirate.


00:45:11.575 --> 00:45:15.510
I don't say this often,
but I'm impressed.


00:45:15.512 --> 00:45:18.913
Bring them both to me and
you could be on your way.


00:45:18.915 --> 00:45:20.514
What about the Paladin?


00:45:20.516 --> 00:45:23.917
- What about him?
He's here, too.


00:45:24.421 --> 00:45:26.587
-Good. Kill him.


00:45:27.524 --> 00:45:29.990
Oh, I don't suspect
that he would


00:45:29.992 --> 00:45:31.326
align his considerable might


00:45:31.328 --> 00:45:33.460
with the interest
of the Coalition again.


00:45:33.462 --> 00:45:35.829
Better to remove him
from the board.


00:45:35.831 --> 00:45:37.998
Let him join his brothers!


00:45:38.000 --> 00:45:40.535
-What's in it for me?


00:45:41.837 --> 00:45:42.670
-Excuse me?


00:45:42.672 --> 00:45:47.775
- Our contract was for Corbryn
and the location of Haven.


00:45:47.777 --> 00:45:49.076
I delivered both.


00:45:49.078 --> 00:45:50.311
Everything after that,


00:45:50.313 --> 00:45:53.847
including rescuing
your daughter, is bonus.


00:45:53.849 --> 00:45:56.917
<i>And this? Not my business.</i>


00:45:56.919 --> 00:45:59.086
I'm not your hired killer.


00:45:59.088 --> 00:46:00.454
-Oh, no, no, no, no.


00:46:00.456 --> 00:46:02.689
You're a pirate that is lucky


00:46:02.691 --> 00:46:05.025
she's proven herself
useful thus far.


00:46:05.027 --> 00:46:10.631
For your own good,
I suggest you continue to do so!


00:46:11.800 --> 00:46:13.867
Wait for me there!


00:46:22.745 --> 00:46:26.046
- All right, let's talk...
alone.


00:46:26.048 --> 00:46:30.416
- Now I warned you...
- Yeah, yeah, I'm warned.


00:46:32.521 --> 00:46:34.620
You coming?


00:46:46.835 --> 00:46:49.469
- I think I've known your dad
for long enough now


00:46:49.471 --> 00:46:52.004
to get why you're
willing to go rebel.


00:46:52.006 --> 00:46:56.476
What I don't get is
how you think you can win.


00:46:56.478 --> 00:46:59.379
- Because we have to
or people will die.


00:46:59.381 --> 00:47:01.814
- Yeah, but what's
your stake in it?


00:47:01.816 --> 00:47:04.951
Coalition's been taking
exactly everything it wants


00:47:04.953 --> 00:47:08.654
since cycles before
either of us were born.


00:47:08.656 --> 00:47:10.155
I'm here because
I didn't have an option.


00:47:10.157 --> 00:47:14.160
Why are you willing to go
to war with your own family


00:47:14.162 --> 00:47:16.528
over a planet
you've never been to?


00:47:16.530 --> 00:47:18.731
- Because I didn't have
a choice either.


00:47:18.733 --> 00:47:20.633
I've known about
Haven my entire life.


00:47:20.635 --> 00:47:22.968
Now that I'm here,
I can't just stand by


00:47:22.970 --> 00:47:25.537
and watch my father destroy it.


00:47:26.039 --> 00:47:27.673
Neither should you.


00:47:27.675 --> 00:47:30.041
-And I'm supposed to do what?


00:47:34.648 --> 00:47:37.183
- Ajax, you have a crew,
you have a ship.


00:47:37.185 --> 00:47:41.453
You can make a difference if
you decide to work with us.


00:47:41.455 --> 00:47:42.587
-Truth is, I don't care.


00:47:42.589 --> 00:47:45.190
I was just trying to get
you away from the Paladin.


00:47:45.192 --> 00:47:46.425
We're leaving.


00:47:46.427 --> 00:47:47.459
-No! We can't leave!


00:47:47.461 --> 00:47:49.461
Thousands will die if
we don't do something!


00:47:49.463 --> 00:47:52.864
- I am doing something!
Hurry up!


00:47:56.570 --> 00:47:58.103
-Denz.


00:48:03.444 --> 00:48:04.576
-Hello?


00:48:04.578 --> 00:48:07.045
What's going on?
Helper, is that you?


00:48:07.748 --> 00:48:10.849
I can hear you.


00:48:14.488 --> 00:48:16.855
-You're in my seat!


00:48:16.924 --> 00:48:19.124
- They're going to find
you, you know.


00:48:19.126 --> 00:48:21.025
-Quiet, princess.


00:48:21.828 --> 00:48:23.861
-Plan B! Plan B!


00:48:23.863 --> 00:48:25.864
-Thank you, Helper.


00:48:29.570 --> 00:48:31.635
-This way!


00:48:33.739 --> 00:48:34.872
-Two of you with me!


00:48:34.874 --> 00:48:40.110
The rest of you,
kill the Paladin.


00:48:43.716 --> 00:48:45.516
-Where are they taking them?


00:48:45.518 --> 00:48:46.884
-She's running away.


00:48:46.886 --> 00:48:49.687
You go. I'll find her.


00:48:52.892 --> 00:48:55.092
-Do not fire that weapon!


00:49:08.207 --> 00:49:10.941
-Do you yield?


00:49:10.943 --> 00:49:13.911
-2,756 Novaks


00:49:13.913 --> 00:49:15.646
perished by these hands


00:49:15.648 --> 00:49:21.118
for this Novak to
stand before you today!


00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:25.822
This Novak does not yield!


00:49:26.859 --> 00:49:28.758
-Very well, then.


00:49:30.129 --> 00:49:32.762
Ready when you are.


00:49:49.215 --> 00:49:51.714
-Pardon my reach.


00:50:08.800 --> 00:50:10.700
What do I do with this?


00:50:10.702 --> 00:50:12.902
-Don't touch it!


00:50:12.904 --> 00:50:15.972
- I'm sure I can find Haven
without you.


00:50:15.974 --> 00:50:17.673
-Good luck!


00:50:36.260 --> 00:50:38.127
-We have to go back!


00:50:39.229 --> 00:50:40.095
-Back? To what?


00:50:40.097 --> 00:50:42.831
A blast like that's gonna bring
the Coalition in no time.


00:50:42.833 --> 00:50:44.099
We have to be gone before then.


00:50:44.101 --> 00:50:46.201
- He could still be alive!
- Then he can find us!


00:50:46.203 --> 00:50:49.338
It's too risky and
not when your dad needs us


00:50:49.340 --> 00:50:50.272
both to win the war.


00:50:50.274 --> 00:50:51.873
-Denz could still be alive.


00:50:51.875 --> 00:50:55.243
- It's too risky!
I'm sorry.


00:51:21.405 --> 00:51:23.305
- I cleared the Bounty.
This is what's left.


00:51:23.307 --> 00:51:27.275
The pirate wasn't lying.
They were definitely here.


00:51:27.277 --> 00:51:28.943
-I see.


00:51:28.945 --> 00:51:29.945
Where are they now?


00:51:29.947 --> 00:51:31.779
- We're still
searching the wreckage,


00:51:31.781 --> 00:51:34.882
but the hold was filled
with crates full of this.


00:51:34.884 --> 00:51:38.419
They're planning on
making a run with it.


00:51:38.421 --> 00:51:40.022
-What is it?


00:51:40.024 --> 00:51:40.821
-It's a battery.


00:51:40.823 --> 00:51:42.758
The power source
is something non-cataloged.


00:51:42.760 --> 00:51:44.959
Can't get a reading on it,
but whatever it is,


00:51:44.961 --> 00:51:49.830
the radiation matches the blast
scoring we found on the Bounty.


00:51:50.233 --> 00:51:52.334
-A weapon! Well, then...


00:51:52.336 --> 00:51:54.802
Each one of you is guilty
of high crimes


00:51:54.804 --> 00:51:57.304
against the Coalition
of the Planets,


00:51:57.306 --> 00:51:59.907
rendering your lives forfeit


00:51:59.909 --> 00:52:05.079
unless one of you should
choose to do the right thing


00:52:05.081 --> 00:52:08.883
and aid us in the war effort.


00:52:09.452 --> 00:52:15.156
- If not for your Coalition,
this Novak would not exist!


00:52:15.158 --> 00:52:19.126
His guilt is your own.


00:52:19.128 --> 00:52:21.829
He will die silently


00:52:21.831 --> 00:52:23.463
before he forfeits his knowledge


00:52:23.465 --> 00:52:26.833
to such feeble men as you!


00:52:28.104 --> 00:52:31.872
I demand trial by combat!


00:52:32.874 --> 00:52:35.443
Name this one your champion


00:52:35.445 --> 00:52:40.113
so I may bring an end
to his days.


00:52:41.217 --> 00:52:46.786
- A Novak, a clone
bred for battle,


00:52:46.788 --> 00:52:48.855
discontinued line.


00:52:48.857 --> 00:52:50.357
He's no threat.


00:52:50.359 --> 00:52:55.428
- How many Novaks
have you killed?


00:52:55.430 --> 00:52:58.064
-None... yet.


00:52:58.066 --> 00:53:02.368
-Then release me and try!


00:53:05.440 --> 00:53:07.107
-I don't see your captain,


00:53:07.109 --> 00:53:12.045
so I'll assume
she's dead or fled.


00:53:12.047 --> 00:53:14.814
And that you are in charge now.


00:53:14.816 --> 00:53:18.951
- Novaks don't command.
They only follow.


00:53:18.953 --> 00:53:23.223
If she's alive, then
he's still under her command.


00:53:23.225 --> 00:53:24.457
-What are the orders, then?


00:53:24.459 --> 00:53:28.026
Where is your captain
and the rebel leader?


00:53:28.028 --> 00:53:30.430
Where is my daughter?


00:53:31.265 --> 00:53:34.399
They were seen with
a man named Denz.


00:53:34.401 --> 00:53:35.869
Perhaps you've seen him,


00:53:35.871 --> 00:53:40.405
a Paladin, like one Novak,
but as strong as 100 Novaks!


00:53:40.407 --> 00:53:43.776
He would make more
than a worthy opponent.


00:53:43.778 --> 00:53:47.846
-No such Novak exists!


00:53:48.884 --> 00:53:51.450
- Was he the one that
destroyed your ship?


00:53:52.120 --> 00:53:55.088
Did he have my daughter
with him?


00:54:02.029 --> 00:54:05.898
-That is one you are owed!


00:54:08.269 --> 00:54:11.336
- You're in no position
to make demands, clone!


00:54:11.338 --> 00:54:14.206
What you owe me has fled
this ship,


00:54:14.208 --> 00:54:16.041
which puts the fate


00:54:16.043 --> 00:54:20.813
in your remaining crew
in your hands, Captain!


00:54:20.815 --> 00:54:23.581
I suggest you consider
how best to be an asset


00:54:23.583 --> 00:54:27.386
to the Coalition in
the upcoming battle.


00:54:28.322 --> 00:54:31.490
Have them taken to the Brig
and search the wreckage.


00:54:31.492 --> 00:54:34.159
Commandeer every last
remaining ship.


00:54:34.161 --> 00:54:37.396
I want to make
certain, absolutely certain,


00:54:37.398 --> 00:54:43.302
that Astera has not
swayed Ajax's loyalties.


00:54:43.604 --> 00:54:45.203
No more tricks.


00:54:45.205 --> 00:54:47.505
Just find them.


00:54:53.047 --> 00:54:54.512
-Move it!


00:54:57.517 --> 00:54:59.518
Clean him up.


00:55:11.364 --> 00:55:13.898
- What do we do
about the Captain?


00:55:13.900 --> 00:55:14.999
-Leave her.


00:55:15.001 --> 00:55:17.435
She's not Captain
of anything now.


00:55:32.252 --> 00:55:35.086
How does all this
still have power?


00:55:35.088 --> 00:55:38.021
-I have to show you something.


00:55:54.607 --> 00:55:57.107
We think the planet
formed around it.


00:55:57.109 --> 00:55:59.676
But it's impossible to get
an accurate date.


00:55:59.678 --> 00:56:02.579
What we do know is
that this is the source


00:56:02.581 --> 00:56:06.249
of everything that
makes Haven a haven.


00:56:06.251 --> 00:56:13.123
The Mana, the distortion effect,
the cloaking field, everything.


00:56:13.926 --> 00:56:16.226
We can't let
the Coalition find it.


00:56:16.228 --> 00:56:18.628
It's limitless
resource and power.


00:56:18.630 --> 00:56:22.465
No one would ever be able
to stand up to them again.


00:56:22.467 --> 00:56:23.600
If they don't take it,


00:56:23.602 --> 00:56:27.470
they'll destroy it,
Haven along with it.


00:56:37.282 --> 00:56:41.083
- Okay, we're stuck here,
so let's talk strategy.


00:56:41.085 --> 00:56:42.551
Helper, how many
ships do we have,


00:56:42.553 --> 00:56:45.421
working ones, functioning ones?


00:56:45.423 --> 00:56:48.123
-Oh, there's got to be...


00:56:48.125 --> 00:56:49.659
-117.


00:56:49.661 --> 00:56:51.427
-Oh.


00:56:51.429 --> 00:56:53.330
That's more than
I thought, actually.


00:56:53.332 --> 00:56:56.465
- It's not enough.
- No.


00:56:56.467 --> 00:56:58.667
- I mean, all we have to do
is take out the warship.


00:56:58.669 --> 00:57:01.103
-Oh, is that it?


00:57:01.973 --> 00:57:04.039
- We don't have enough ships
for a direct assault.


00:57:04.041 --> 00:57:07.676
But maybe they can
buy us some time.


00:57:10.548 --> 00:57:13.148
-Time for what?


00:57:15.018 --> 00:57:15.751
-We don't have Denz,


00:57:15.753 --> 00:57:18.052
but we have a ship and
we have the Mana bomb.


00:57:18.054 --> 00:57:20.622
You guys saw what it did
to the Bounty.


00:57:20.624 --> 00:57:24.525
Maybe if we get
onboard the warship...


00:57:25.096 --> 00:57:27.029
I don't know...
maybe we can...


00:57:27.031 --> 00:57:28.030
-Astera?


00:57:28.032 --> 00:57:32.568
The people who came to Haven,
they're not fighters.


00:57:32.570 --> 00:57:35.004
They're not leaders.


00:57:35.006 --> 00:57:36.238
Look what they did.


00:57:36.240 --> 00:57:38.540
They turned a warship
into a warehouse.


00:57:38.542 --> 00:57:41.443
If we send them into
a battle they can't win...


00:57:41.445 --> 00:57:46.314
- We can win.
We just need a plan.


00:57:47.485 --> 00:57:49.450
-Maybe.


00:57:49.452 --> 00:57:53.221
Maybe Haven does need a leader.


00:57:53.223 --> 00:57:55.790
- Corbryn,
you're Haven's leader.


00:57:55.792 --> 00:57:57.626
I mean, you've gotten
them this far.


00:57:57.628 --> 00:58:01.462
Just keep doing
what you're doing. Don't even...


00:58:01.464 --> 00:58:02.597
What's that?


00:58:02.599 --> 00:58:03.297
-Huh?


00:58:03.299 --> 00:58:06.167
Oh, just one of
the many uses of Mana.


00:58:06.169 --> 00:58:07.235
These are traveler's tokens.


00:58:07.237 --> 00:58:09.237
They hold the records
of the ones who came,


00:58:09.239 --> 00:58:11.773
how they got here,
where they came from.


00:58:11.775 --> 00:58:13.241
-Do they work?


00:58:13.243 --> 00:58:15.543
-Yeah.


00:58:15.545 --> 00:58:18.579
Where did you get that?


00:58:18.581 --> 00:58:20.248
-From my mom.


00:58:20.250 --> 00:58:21.382
She died trying to get here.


00:58:21.384 --> 00:58:23.584
Must have been one of the
distress beacons


00:58:23.586 --> 00:58:25.286
that Denz missed.


00:58:25.288 --> 00:58:27.822
Just another reason
to hate the Coalition.


00:58:27.824 --> 00:58:30.324
-Are you sure...


00:58:30.627 --> 00:58:32.392
you want to?


00:58:33.096 --> 00:58:35.195
-I have to.


00:58:42.705 --> 00:58:45.505
<i>- There's no time!
They're coming!</i>


00:58:45.507 --> 00:58:46.474
What is this?


00:58:46.476 --> 00:58:49.410
<i>- I need you to help her!
Stay with her!</i>


00:58:49.412 --> 00:58:52.713
- The program's been wiped
from my memory.


00:58:52.782 --> 00:58:57.250
<i>- Keep her safe, okay?
Promise me!</i>


00:58:57.519 --> 00:59:00.353
<i>Make sure she knows.</i>


00:59:00.355 --> 00:59:02.622
<i>Make sure she knows I love her.</i>


00:59:02.624 --> 00:59:07.327
<i>You... You can record.</i>


00:59:09.565 --> 00:59:16.169
<i>Astera, it may take a long time
for you to understand this.</i>


00:59:16.171 --> 00:59:18.772
That's my mom.


00:59:18.774 --> 00:59:24.845
<i>I want a better life for you
and I tried for that,</i>


00:59:24.847 --> 00:59:27.346
<i>but I failed.</i>


00:59:28.150 --> 00:59:30.416
<i>I need you.</i>


00:59:30.651 --> 00:59:35.388
<i>If your father were to ever
find Haven, he will destroy!</i>


00:59:36.190 --> 00:59:41.328
<i>I hate to burden you with this.
You're still so young.</i>


00:59:41.330 --> 00:59:45.631
<i>But one day,
you will have to remember</i>


00:59:45.633 --> 00:59:48.801
<i>that no life is worth a planet,</i>


00:59:48.803 --> 00:59:53.507
<i>not mine, not his,</i>


00:59:53.509 --> 00:59:55.541
<i>not even yours.</i>


00:59:56.511 --> 00:59:58.410
<i>Promise me.</i>


00:59:59.814 --> 01:00:01.714
<i>I love you.</i>


01:00:04.418 --> 01:00:05.718
-What's happening?


01:00:05.720 --> 01:00:07.219
Helper?


01:00:07.221 --> 01:00:10.656
-Astera, look away.


01:00:14.862 --> 01:00:16.695
-Who would...


01:00:16.697 --> 01:00:17.496
Zelus!


01:00:17.498 --> 01:00:21.734
- Citizens of Haven!
The deadline has expired!


01:00:21.736 --> 01:00:22.668
-We're out of time.


01:00:22.670 --> 01:00:25.905
- Send forth your representative
and prepare for surrender


01:00:25.907 --> 01:00:29.675
or face the full power
of the Coalition!


01:00:31.312 --> 01:00:34.412
- What's that?
- That's my ship!


01:00:35.449 --> 01:00:37.482
My ship!


01:00:51.933 --> 01:00:53.565
-I told you, fiend!


01:00:53.567 --> 01:00:58.970
I made a promise to protect
this planet and its people,


01:00:58.972 --> 01:01:02.907
and another,
to avenge my brothers...


01:01:02.909 --> 01:01:05.643
and I intend to keep both.


01:01:05.645 --> 01:01:08.947
-Paladin, you can barely stand.


01:01:08.949 --> 01:01:14.352
-And yet I stand with them.


01:01:19.793 --> 01:01:22.360
-Open fire!


01:01:23.463 --> 01:01:26.364
-Corbryn, it's now or never.


01:01:27.534 --> 01:01:28.766
-Attention all ships!


01:01:28.768 --> 01:01:31.603
Anyone on this band, anyone
who can hear me, attack!


01:01:31.605 --> 01:01:36.473
Get your asses in the air
and fight to save your planet!


01:02:10.009 --> 01:02:10.874
-Is it bad?


01:02:10.876 --> 01:02:13.844
Oh, yeah, it's bad, isn't it?


01:02:13.846 --> 01:02:15.879
Check the box.


01:02:15.881 --> 01:02:16.880
-What box?


01:02:16.882 --> 01:02:19.583
-The green metal one.


01:02:30.596 --> 01:02:32.429
They'll come for it.


01:02:32.431 --> 01:02:35.465
- We gotta get out of here.
- I'm ready.


01:02:38.704 --> 01:02:42.572
- Corbryn, snap out of it!
We have to get out of here!


01:02:42.574 --> 01:02:44.040
- No, they'll come
for the Mana core!


01:02:44.042 --> 01:02:47.043
- Corbryn, the battle's
out there now!


01:02:47.045 --> 01:02:48.945
We have to leave!


01:02:48.947 --> 01:02:52.349
Okay, let's go!


01:02:52.351 --> 01:02:54.985
Helper?
- Go!


01:02:56.888 --> 01:02:59.422
I'll hold them off!


01:03:00.425 --> 01:03:04.461
<i>What's happening down there?</i>


01:03:04.763 --> 01:03:05.628
-They attacked!


01:03:05.630 --> 01:03:06.962
Peace was offered and declined!


01:03:06.964 --> 01:03:09.899
I had no choice but to respond!


01:03:10.034 --> 01:03:12.435
- Zelus, I told you
to hold until I gave...


01:03:12.437 --> 01:03:14.737
- They have the Paladin
with them!


01:03:14.739 --> 01:03:16.739
If I hold, I die!


01:03:20.011 --> 01:03:22.078
Continue the attack!


01:03:22.080 --> 01:03:24.013
-Bring us in now.


01:03:26.117 --> 01:03:27.883
-Astera!


01:03:31.756 --> 01:03:34.457
Your father wants to see you.


01:04:26.910 --> 01:04:28.410
Yield.


01:04:28.412 --> 01:04:29.844
-Never.


01:04:48.799 --> 01:04:51.900
- I see the champion
still stands.


01:04:51.902 --> 01:04:55.502
Show them what happens when
you defy the Coalition.


01:04:55.504 --> 01:04:57.806
Make him surrender.


01:04:57.808 --> 01:05:00.775
Fire the tractor beam.


01:05:17.493 --> 01:05:18.091
-Bastard!


01:05:18.093 --> 01:05:20.694
What? Are you gonna kill me
like you killed her, too?


01:05:26.535 --> 01:05:28.902
-Let her go!


01:05:29.605 --> 01:05:31.038
-You killed her.


01:05:31.040 --> 01:05:36.810
She tried to run,
like you tried to kill me.


01:05:36.812 --> 01:05:37.678
But you can't.


01:05:37.680 --> 01:05:42.014
- I didn't kill your
traitor of a mother,


01:05:42.016 --> 01:05:45.719
though I gladly would
have for what she did!


01:05:54.162 --> 01:05:55.796
-Then who?


01:05:55.798 --> 01:05:59.066
-I suggest you ask your father.


01:06:03.204 --> 01:06:05.506
-Dad, stop!


01:06:05.508 --> 01:06:10.843
- Astera, I'm so glad to
see that you're safe.


01:06:10.845 --> 01:06:12.612
It pleases me how
integral you were


01:06:12.614 --> 01:06:15.015
to the Coalition's
victory here today.


01:06:15.017 --> 01:06:18.151
- Dad, let him go.
Please.


01:06:18.153 --> 01:06:20.253
-He chose the wrong side.


01:06:20.255 --> 01:06:24.957
You, on the other hand,
have managed to elude capture


01:06:24.959 --> 01:06:26.993
and deliver not only
the rebel leader,


01:06:26.995 --> 01:06:28.961
but the location of
their hidden base,


01:06:28.963 --> 01:06:34.033
and the very source
of their power.


01:06:34.035 --> 01:06:37.637
Quite a resource
kept hidden so long.


01:06:37.639 --> 01:06:40.038
It would have brought
great advancements


01:06:40.040 --> 01:06:41.040
to the Coalition effort


01:06:41.042 --> 01:06:45.845
if you had not kept it for
your own selfish needs.


01:06:45.847 --> 01:06:50.048
- Guess I thought
the Coalition had enough power.


01:06:50.050 --> 01:06:51.784
-You thought wrong.


01:06:51.786 --> 01:06:54.220
I understand you're
in possession of a frequency


01:06:54.222 --> 01:06:56.989
we use to calibrate
our instruments


01:06:56.991 --> 01:07:00.293
to extract the source.


01:07:00.295 --> 01:07:02.027
-It's not gonna happen.


01:07:02.029 --> 01:07:04.996
-Oh? I see.


01:07:09.269 --> 01:07:10.002
-Stop!


01:07:10.004 --> 01:07:13.838
-The Paladin is neutralized,


01:07:13.840 --> 01:07:18.143
your fleet decimated,
base is in ruins!


01:07:18.145 --> 01:07:19.945
And the battle already lost.


01:07:19.947 --> 01:07:25.150
You can choose to be the leader
Haven needs right now!


01:07:25.152 --> 01:07:26.651
You can stop the war!


01:07:26.653 --> 01:07:30.589
You can save what's left
of the refugees, or...


01:07:30.591 --> 01:07:33.658
You can watch as
I obliterate this planet.


01:07:33.660 --> 01:07:37.996
Give me the rebel frequency
and surrender!


01:07:38.665 --> 01:07:42.000
End this.
Full-scale assault, planet wide.


01:07:42.002 --> 01:07:46.338
We'll just have to extract
the core from the rubble.


01:07:48.107 --> 01:07:49.741
-No! Wait!


01:07:49.743 --> 01:07:50.641
-Corbryn!


01:07:50.643 --> 01:07:53.111
-Wait! Stop!


01:07:53.113 --> 01:07:55.280
-Cease fire.


01:07:58.919 --> 01:08:01.219
-It's the people or the planet.


01:08:16.702 --> 01:08:18.736
-It worked.


01:08:20.106 --> 01:08:22.172
-Begin extraction.


01:08:23.342 --> 01:08:25.743
-No! No, wait!


01:08:25.745 --> 01:08:26.744
I surrendered!


01:08:26.746 --> 01:08:30.314
There's people down there!
You said refugees...


01:08:30.316 --> 01:08:35.686
- They stopped being refugees
when the deadline expired.


01:08:35.688 --> 01:08:36.920
You had your chance.


01:08:36.922 --> 01:08:40.057
- You liar!
- Do it.


01:08:58.176 --> 01:08:59.877
-Denz!


01:09:00.979 --> 01:09:04.180
- The Paladin
makes an appearance.


01:09:15.961 --> 01:09:18.061
-Denz!


01:09:18.163 --> 01:09:20.229
- Put the rebel leader
with the rest


01:09:20.231 --> 01:09:22.699
of the criminals in the Brig.


01:09:22.701 --> 01:09:23.966
-And the Paladin?


01:09:23.968 --> 01:09:26.302
- He won't make any
further difference here.


01:09:26.304 --> 01:09:29.772
He did the worst of
his damage a long time ago.


01:09:29.774 --> 01:09:31.207
-Kill him?


01:09:31.209 --> 01:09:34.977
-No! Dad, please!


01:09:37.881 --> 01:09:39.382
-Put him back in his ship.


01:09:39.384 --> 01:09:42.418
Make sure that
he's in hyper sleep.


01:09:42.420 --> 01:09:46.189
Oh, and make sure he has a view.


01:09:46.357 --> 01:09:47.789
Perhaps in a thousand cycles,


01:09:47.791 --> 01:09:50.258
he will have atoned
for his betrayal.


01:09:53.263 --> 01:09:56.032
-Let's go.


01:09:56.034 --> 01:09:58.468
You, too.


01:09:58.470 --> 01:10:00.870
Move!


01:10:07.946 --> 01:10:11.414
Don't try anything stupid.


01:10:17.522 --> 01:10:19.955
<i>I have to say,
Paladin, I had hoped</i>


01:10:19.957 --> 01:10:21.189
<i>things would end differently.</i>


01:10:21.191 --> 01:10:22.457
<i>See you in a thousand cycles.</i>


01:10:22.459 --> 01:10:24.359
<i>- No! No!
- Hypersleep sequence initiated.</i>


01:10:24.361 --> 01:10:28.430
- Squire! Cancel!
Open the door!


01:10:29.233 --> 01:10:31.399
- Dad...
- We will speak later.


01:10:31.401 --> 01:10:35.403
Until then, I expect you
to remain in your quarters.


01:10:35.405 --> 01:10:38.840
- Are you really
sending me to my room?


01:10:38.842 --> 01:10:42.144
- There are
far worse alternatives.


01:10:42.146 --> 01:10:45.513
I hope you know how much
I strive to keep you


01:10:45.515 --> 01:10:49.484
from being suspected of more
than childish rebelliousness!


01:10:49.486 --> 01:10:53.388
I hope you know
that everything I've done


01:10:53.390 --> 01:10:56.124
has been to protect you!


01:10:56.126 --> 01:10:58.159
-From who, Dad?


01:10:58.161 --> 01:10:59.494
Your Coalition?


01:10:59.496 --> 01:11:01.228
What does that tell you?


01:11:01.230 --> 01:11:05.534
- Like it or not, we are the
force of order in the galaxy.


01:11:05.536 --> 01:11:11.005
I'd hoped you'd learn that
sooner than your mother did.


01:11:11.007 --> 01:11:15.977
Please don't repeat
her mistakes.


01:11:19.348 --> 01:11:21.081
-Sure.


01:11:29.592 --> 01:11:34.562
- Hey, guys,
wanna blow this joint?


01:11:35.565 --> 01:11:39.099
<i>- Do you have access to Honor?
- -They're jamming my signal.</i>


01:11:39.101 --> 01:11:40.234
<i>I can't get inside.</i>


01:11:40.236 --> 01:11:41.302
-Can you reach it from here?


01:11:41.304 --> 01:11:43.037
<i>- I can try.
- Do it.</i>


01:11:43.039 --> 01:11:46.507
Let Denz keep them busy.
I'll get Corbryn.


01:11:47.543 --> 01:11:49.310
-Open the door!


01:12:08.164 --> 01:12:10.097
<i>Captain Ajax, can you hear me?</i>


01:12:10.099 --> 01:12:13.032
<i>Captain Ajax, are you there?</i>


01:12:13.369 --> 01:12:17.137
- Yeah, I hear you.
Hold on.


01:12:23.479 --> 01:12:26.513
-That was using your head.


01:12:27.415 --> 01:12:29.450
No hard feelings?


01:12:30.452 --> 01:12:34.254
-No more tricks?


01:12:34.256 --> 01:12:36.322
-No more tricks.


01:12:37.058 --> 01:12:41.027
-This should work... I think.


01:12:41.296 --> 01:12:44.964
- Get off your asses!
It's time to fight!


01:12:44.966 --> 01:12:45.899
-2,756 Novaks...


01:12:45.901 --> 01:12:47.567
- Yeah, yeah, yeah, a lot
of Novaks... it's all right.


01:12:47.569 --> 01:12:49.135
I got it.
Here, let's get out of here.


01:12:49.137 --> 01:12:52.572
- He's coming.
I'll show you the way!


01:12:53.141 --> 01:12:54.406
-Astera, what about you?


01:12:54.408 --> 01:12:55.608
-I'll disable the tractor beam.


01:12:55.610 --> 01:12:57.076
- What if...
- Shut up!


01:12:57.078 --> 01:12:58.410
I know this ship
better than anyone.


01:12:58.412 --> 01:12:59.479
I can get around faster.


01:12:59.481 --> 01:13:02.148
- Yeah, but what about...
- Don't worry about me!


01:13:02.150 --> 01:13:03.216
You're their leader now,


01:13:03.218 --> 01:13:07.219
so get out there and lead
and let's win this thing.


01:13:12.993 --> 01:13:14.694
- I need to get
into that warship.


01:13:14.696 --> 01:13:17.596
- No way they're gonna
let us dock now.


01:13:18.433 --> 01:13:20.232
- They wouldn't have to
if it wasn't


01:13:20.234 --> 01:13:22.267
for the damage to
this blasted armor.


01:13:22.269 --> 01:13:24.036
My battery's almost depleted.


01:13:24.038 --> 01:13:29.508
- You kidding me?
We got all the power you need.


01:13:33.447 --> 01:13:36.048
-Let's hope this works.


01:13:36.550 --> 01:13:40.185
-Like mother, like daughter!


01:13:40.187 --> 01:13:41.586
-I'm...


01:13:48.062 --> 01:13:49.994
-Zelus!


01:13:49.996 --> 01:13:52.264
-Hello, Paladin!


01:13:52.266 --> 01:13:54.099
-That's enough!


01:13:56.502 --> 01:13:59.003
- Out of all the Paladins
I've killed,


01:13:59.005 --> 01:14:02.640
your death is going to be
the one I enjoy the most.


01:14:21.728 --> 01:14:23.694
-This one's for Haven!


01:14:36.509 --> 01:14:38.075
Denz...?


01:14:39.479 --> 01:14:41.212
-Are you all right?


01:14:41.214 --> 01:14:41.746
-Yeah.


01:14:41.748 --> 01:14:45.583
There's just one more
thing I have to do.


01:14:46.586 --> 01:14:50.621
I'll meet you at your ship.


01:14:50.623 --> 01:14:54.591
Dad! Come out here!
- Astera?


01:14:57.096 --> 01:14:58.195
Is this what you wanted?


01:14:58.197 --> 01:14:59.764
Destroying an entire planet,


01:14:59.766 --> 01:15:01.732
killing thousands
of innocent people?


01:15:01.734 --> 01:15:05.436
- They stole the ship
that brought them here.


01:15:05.438 --> 01:15:08.606
They stole the resources
to fuel it.


01:15:08.608 --> 01:15:09.706
From the moment of its founding,


01:15:09.708 --> 01:15:13.109
this planet has been nothing
but a malignant tumor


01:15:13.111 --> 01:15:16.212
feeding off the lifeblood
of the Coalition.


01:15:16.214 --> 01:15:20.550
And now that tumor
has been removed.


01:15:20.552 --> 01:15:21.485
-No.


01:15:21.487 --> 01:15:22.685
I don't think it was the tumor.


01:15:22.687 --> 01:15:27.725
I think you just can't stand
to see people free.


01:15:27.727 --> 01:15:29.192
-Astera, come on...


01:15:29.194 --> 01:15:30.694
-No, don't.


01:15:32.197 --> 01:15:34.731
You don't get
to do that anymore.


01:15:36.736 --> 01:15:39.636
I have a ship ready and waiting.


01:15:40.505 --> 01:15:41.471
I just need to, um...


01:15:41.473 --> 01:15:46.142
I just need to know
one thing about Mom.


01:15:46.511 --> 01:15:49.645
You said she died
trying to get to Haven.


01:15:50.749 --> 01:15:52.781
-That's right.


01:15:52.783 --> 01:15:54.150
-But she got there.


01:15:54.152 --> 01:15:57.454
She just never
made it back, right?


01:15:57.456 --> 01:16:00.757
- Astera, don't ask...
- Was it you?


01:16:02.393 --> 01:16:04.360
- I loved your mother very much.


01:16:04.362 --> 01:16:06.129
-Did you kill her?


01:16:06.131 --> 01:16:07.363
-She betrayed me!


01:16:07.365 --> 01:16:10.366
You! She betrayed us all!


01:16:10.368 --> 01:16:12.234
-Did you?


01:16:13.405 --> 01:16:15.538
-She had an option.


01:16:15.540 --> 01:16:17.139
She chose her path!


01:16:17.141 --> 01:16:22.245
I didn't want to do it,
but she forced my hand!


01:16:25.617 --> 01:16:30.252
Your mother made her own choice.


01:16:32.257 --> 01:16:37.259
-Yeah, and I've made mine.


01:16:41.532 --> 01:16:43.432
-Astera...


01:16:45.469 --> 01:16:47.469
Then you'll die with
the rest of them.


01:16:47.471 --> 01:16:50.705
<i>Sir, the rebel fleet is out.</i>


01:16:50.707 --> 01:16:53.509
Release the fighters.


01:16:57.781 --> 01:16:59.348
<i>Calling all ships!</i>


01:16:59.350 --> 01:17:00.681
That's your planet's
heart down there!


01:17:00.683 --> 01:17:03.217
Let's pull it together
and end this thing.


01:17:03.219 --> 01:17:03.885
Everyone on me!


01:17:03.887 --> 01:17:04.920
<i>We're with you!</i>


01:17:04.922 --> 01:17:07.289
<i>Watch your backs.
Here they come!</i>


01:17:07.291 --> 01:17:09.257
-Get them!


01:17:11.595 --> 01:17:12.660
-You got one behind you!


01:17:12.662 --> 01:17:16.264
- He's locked on to me.
I'm going to try to lose him.


01:17:16.266 --> 01:17:17.332
A little help would be nice.


01:17:17.334 --> 01:17:20.469
- Hang in there.
Twell's on him.


01:17:22.639 --> 01:17:25.640
<i>If you have it, take the shot.</i>


01:17:25.642 --> 01:17:27.542
<i>Fire!</i>


01:17:30.314 --> 01:17:32.446
<i>Whoa! Nice shot!</i>


01:17:32.515 --> 01:17:35.216
<i>Okay, I'm going for the beam.
Cover me.</i>


01:17:35.218 --> 01:17:37.451
We're on you.


01:17:40.924 --> 01:17:41.956
<i>Whoa! Yeah!</i>


01:17:41.958 --> 01:17:44.825
That tractor beam's down,
but the warship's still kicking!


01:17:44.827 --> 01:17:47.428
We gotta get that Mana core
back down to the surface.


01:17:47.430 --> 01:17:48.462
Any ideas?


01:17:48.464 --> 01:17:50.264
<i>I might have one.</i>


01:17:50.266 --> 01:17:53.401
- Great. We could use
a pirate trick right now.


01:17:53.403 --> 01:17:56.470
<i>I got just the thing,
but I got to get a signal out.</i>


01:17:56.472 --> 01:17:58.572
<i>You'll have to give
me the frequency.</i>


01:17:58.574 --> 01:18:02.743
- That I can do.
Sending it now.


01:18:02.745 --> 01:18:04.378
-Oh, I got it.


01:18:04.380 --> 01:18:07.681
<i>- I hope this works.
- So do I.</i>


01:18:07.683 --> 01:18:11.886
Come on, baby.
One last jump.


01:18:13.655 --> 01:18:21.428
Prepare for impact.
In three... two... one.


01:18:21.965 --> 01:18:26.299
Yeah! Ramming speed, baby!


01:18:27.436 --> 01:18:30.003
Oh, sorry.


01:18:30.005 --> 01:18:32.706
Wait. The Mana core
isn't moving.


01:18:32.708 --> 01:18:35.009
- It's already escaped the
planet's gravitational pull.


01:18:35.011 --> 01:18:36.910
<i>You're
going to have to use that ship</i>


01:18:36.912 --> 01:18:39.546
<i>and push it back down.</i>


01:18:39.548 --> 01:18:41.848
- The ship's only got
one pod left.


01:18:41.850 --> 01:18:44.718
Take it, get to safety.
When I'm done here, hopefully,


01:18:44.720 --> 01:18:46.886
there will still be planet
left for me to land on.


01:18:46.888 --> 01:18:49.723
-That's all I needed to hear.


01:18:50.926 --> 01:18:51.825
You coming?


01:18:51.827 --> 01:18:53.426
- What are you doing?
Are you not coming?


01:18:53.428 --> 01:18:56.729
- Someone needs to stay
if this doesn't work.


01:18:56.731 --> 01:18:57.530
-It'll work.


01:18:57.532 --> 01:18:59.566
- Then I'll see you
on the surface.


01:18:59.568 --> 01:19:02.502
- I'm not gonna
leave you here alone.


01:19:02.504 --> 01:19:03.670
-Ahem.


01:19:03.672 --> 01:19:06.740
He won't be.
I'll stay.


01:19:07.476 --> 01:19:09.842
Not like I have a choice
in the matter anymore.


01:19:09.844 --> 01:19:13.613
Honor holds the last copy
of my programming.


01:19:14.616 --> 01:19:15.714
-Helper, I'm so sorry.


01:19:15.716 --> 01:19:17.751
I completely forgot
that you'll...


01:19:17.753 --> 01:19:19.551
- You'll die.
- Yes.


01:19:19.553 --> 01:19:21.320
- Lucky for you,
self-preservation


01:19:21.322 --> 01:19:24.356
is not a core dictate
of my programming.


01:19:24.492 --> 01:19:26.860
- Thank you, Helper,
for everything.


01:19:26.862 --> 01:19:29.596
- It's been
a considerable pleasure.


01:19:29.598 --> 01:19:33.400
I am, after all, here to help.


01:19:37.638 --> 01:19:42.309
- Commander Corbryn, pull back
and get your people to safety!


01:19:42.311 --> 01:19:44.743
All right,
I thought you'd never ask.


01:19:44.745 --> 01:19:47.780
<i>Give her everything you got!</i>


01:19:53.087 --> 01:19:55.454
-It's not enough!


01:19:59.660 --> 01:20:01.592
-It's not working.


01:20:03.731 --> 01:20:07.598
Helper, I'm sorry.


01:20:07.901 --> 01:20:13.038
Squire, ready the self-destruct
and activate on reentry.


01:20:13.040 --> 01:20:14.873
The blast should be
powerful enough


01:20:14.875 --> 01:20:17.108
to send the Mana core
back to the ground.


01:20:17.110 --> 01:20:20.378
But I will need
to pilot us within range.


01:20:20.380 --> 01:20:21.480
-Denz, allow me.


01:20:21.482 --> 01:20:24.750
You've already sacrificed
yourself once for Haven.


01:20:24.752 --> 01:20:26.351
You don't need to do it again.


01:20:26.353 --> 01:20:28.654
I can handle the ship.


01:20:29.689 --> 01:20:33.992
-Helper, this... this war,


01:20:33.994 --> 01:20:36.561
it's all my fault.


01:20:36.563 --> 01:20:40.866
And the fate of this planet
is my burden to bear.


01:20:40.868 --> 01:20:45.136
<i>Self-destruct
sequence initiated.</i>


01:20:45.138 --> 01:20:47.872
-Not anymore it's not.


01:20:54.013 --> 01:20:55.847
-Thank you, Helper.


01:21:02.888 --> 01:21:08.925
<i>Self-destruct in five,
four, three, two...</i>


01:21:16.503 --> 01:21:18.068
-They did it!


01:21:24.710 --> 01:21:26.911
Denz! You made it!


01:21:26.913 --> 01:21:28.178
-I had some help.


01:21:28.180 --> 01:21:30.147
-Are we all gonna die?


01:21:30.149 --> 01:21:32.082
-Not today.


01:21:32.185 --> 01:21:34.951
I guess you won't be going
into hyper sleep again.


01:21:34.953 --> 01:21:36.453
-I hope not.


01:21:36.455 --> 01:21:37.087
-That's good.


01:21:37.089 --> 01:21:41.859
Haven could use some wisdom from
the ages, healthy perspectives.


01:21:41.861 --> 01:21:44.161
-I guess you're right.


01:21:44.163 --> 01:21:47.130
- The Coalition's
not gonna leave Haven alone,


01:21:47.132 --> 01:21:49.533
not after this.


01:21:49.902 --> 01:21:50.734
-She's right.


01:21:50.736 --> 01:21:52.102
They'll want to know
what happened.


01:21:52.104 --> 01:21:53.103
They'll come looking.


01:21:53.105 --> 01:21:56.673
- And when they do,
we'll be ready.

